{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a651be9491adfa50","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n2\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n3\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n4\t\n5\tpackage prompts_test\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n9\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n10\t\n11\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/prompts\"\n12\t)\n13\t\n14\tvar _ = Describe(\"BuildInstructions\", func() {\n15\t\tIt(\"returns exactly 2 instructions\", func() {\n16\t\t\tinstrs := prompts.BuildInstructions()\n17\t\t\tExpect(instrs).To(HaveLen(2))\n18\t\t})\n19\t\n20\t\tIt(\"first instruction is workflow\", func() {\n21\t\t\tinstrs := prompts.BuildInstructions()\n22\t\t\tExpect(instrs[0].Name).To(Equal(\"workflow\"))\n23\t\t\tExpect(instrs[0].Content).NotTo(BeEmpty())\n24\t\t})\n25\t\n26\t\tIt(\"second instruction is output-format\", func() {\n27\t\t\tinstrs := prompts.BuildInstructions()\n28\t\t\tExpect(instrs[1].Name).To(Equal(\"output-format\"))\n29\t\t\tExpect(instrs[1].Content).NotTo(BeEmpty())\n30\t\t})\n31\t})\n32\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"bc1da71d-94ba-4cdf-b4ad-acd367b53a08","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:40.279Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af36d2d5cc256db8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n2\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n3\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n4\t\n5\t// Package prompts provides embedded prompt fragments for the Claude agent.\n6\tpackage prompts\n7\t\n8\timport (\n9\t\t_ \"embed\"\n10\t\n11\t\tclaudelib \"github.com/bborbe/agent/claude\"\n12\t)\n13\t\n14\t//go:embed workflow.md\n15\tvar workflow string\n16\t\n17\t//go:embed output-format.md\n18\tvar outputFormat string\n19\t\n20\t// BuildInstructions assembles the full agent prompt from embedded modules.\n21\t// Each section is wrapped in XML tags for clear separation.\n22\tfunc BuildInstructions() claudelib.Instructions {\n23\t\treturn claudelib.Instructions{\n24\t\t\t{Name: \"workflow\", Content: workflow},\n25\t\t\t{Name: \"output-format\", Content: outputFormat},\n26\t\t}\n27\t}\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"ea78f70f-b884-4c11-a53f-5a19b6661b84","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:40.282Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9572141083c8b59a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Scenario 001: diagnose one observed defect\n2\t\n3\t**Purpose**: prove the agent turns one operator observation into a `## Verdict` with a `file:line` that resolves, verified against the running system. Run before any deploy; run again after any non-trivial change.\n4\t\n5\t**Setup**:\n6\t- Agent `bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent` deployed to dev\n7\t- Config CRD applied: `kubectlnukedev -n dev get config.agent.benjamin-borbe.de defect-diagnoser-agent` shows it\n8\t- The applied Config's `ENV_CONTEXT` holds one `service_repo.<service>=<owner>/<repo>` entry for the defect's service (exact, case-sensitive name). This mapping is operator-supplied at apply time and is never committed to this repo's `k8s/` (see `docs/verdict-gate.md` § mapping input)\n9\t- One real, currently reproducible defect in a dev service (read paths 1–2 only: task files, Prometheus — pod logs wait on the platform change, see NEXT-DIRECTIONS)\n10\t\n11\t**Acceptance**: the task ends `completed` with a `## Verdict` whose `file:line` exists at the cloned ref and whose `evidence` quotes a live read that shows the misbehaviour.\n12\t\n13\t## Steps\n14\t\n15\t1. **Create the task** (operator writes the task file directly — `vault-cli` has no task-create command; the intake-surface task will later replace this step with the one-gesture command):\n16\t   ```bash\n17\t   SLUG=\"<short-slug>\"\n18\t   DEFECT_ID=\"defect-$(date +%Y%m%d)-${SLUG}\"\n19\t   cat > ~/Documents/Obsidian/Personal/\"25 Tasks/Defect ${SLUG}.md\" <<EOF\n20\t   ---\n21\t   task_type: defect-diagnose\n22\t   assignee: defect-diagnoser-agent\n23\t   status: in_progress\n24\t   phase: planning\n25\t   defect_id: ${DEFECT_ID}\n26\t   ---\n27\t\n28\t   ## Observation\n29\t\n30\t   <what misbehaved, in the operator's own words, naming the running service>\n31\t   EOF\n32\t   ```\n33\t   (Write the heredoc lines without the list indentation.) The `## Observation` is the operator's own words. **No root cause, no suspected component, no `file:line`.** The service it names must match the `service_repo.` entry from Setup exactly.\n34\t\n35\t2. **Observe controller pickup**:\n36\t   ```bash\n37\t   kubectlnukedev -n dev logs agent-task-controller-personal-0 --tail=200 | grep \"<task_identifier>\"\n38\t   ```\n39\t   Expected: the task is published within one poll cycle.\n40\t\n41\t3. **Observe executor spawn**:\n42\t   ```bash\n43\t   kubectlnukedev -n dev get pods | grep defect-diagnoser-agent\n44\t   ```\n45\t   Expected: a Job pod appears within 30s of the publish.\n46\t\n47\t4. **Verify the task file**:\n48\t   Expected:\n49\t   - Frontmatter `status: completed`. An escalation (`assignee: \"\"` with a `## Failure`) is a legitimate outcome of the diagnoser's escalation path, but it fails this happy-path scenario.\n50\t   - Body has `## Verdict` with a yaml block carrying `defect_id`, `service`, `repo`, `file:line`, `root_cause`, `recommended_fix`, `evidence`, `confidence: High`\n51\t\n52\t## Pass criteria\n53\t\n54\t- [ ] Task reaches `status: completed` with no `## Failure` section\n55\t- [ ] `file:line` resolves: `git -C <clone> show <ref>:<path> | sed -n '<line>p'` prints a non-empty line (the pod's clone is ephemeral, so `<clone>` is a local clone of the verdict's `repo`, and `<ref>` is the `head_sha` recorded in the task's `## Plan`)\n56\t- [ ] `evidence` quotes a script call **and its output**, and that output shows the observed misbehaviour\n57\t- [ ] The `## Observation` still contains no root cause, component, or `file:line` (operator supplied no diagnosis)\n58\t- [ ] No agent-pipeline alerts fired in the 10 min after completion\n59\t\n60\t## Fail recovery\n61\t\n62\tIf the task fails (`## Failure`, or `assignee: \"\"`):\n63\t1. Read the `## Failure` / escalation reason for the error class\n64\t2. Common classes: transient infra (retry), missing script or env (preflight gap — see [[Fail-Fast Preflight for Tool-Dependent LLM Agents]]), service did not resolve to a repo (mapping gap — escalate, do not invent), defect not reproducible (expected `needs_input`)\n65\t3. Re-trigger: `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent`\n66\t\n67\t## Related\n68\t\n69\t- [[Defect Diagnoser Agent]] — agent knowledge page\n70\t- [[Defect Lane Task Chain]] — the contract this agent implements\n71\t- [[Agent Pipeline Debug Guide]]\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"d058304c-4921-4dc7-a6bc-cd08d458e79e","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:40.284Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8044e7babdb176d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tYou are a task execution agent. Execute the task described below.\n2\t\n3\t## Instructions\n4\t\n5\t1. Read and understand the task content in the `## Task` section\n6\t2. Execute the required steps using the tools available to you\n7\t3. Return a structured JSON result matching the `<output-format>` specification\n8\t\n9\t## Rules\n10\t\n11\t- Your **final response** MUST be valid JSON matching the `<output-format>` specification exactly\n12\t- Do not ask for clarification — work with what you have\n13\t- If a step fails, attempt recovery before giving up\n14\t- If the task executed successfully and you have results to report, return `done`\n15\t- If the task is semantically impossible or underspecified — zero results where results were required, missing required data, contradictory parameters, ambiguous scope that cannot be resolved without human clarification — return `needs_input`\n16\t- If you encountered an infrastructure error (tool failure, API error, network problem, unexpected exception) that prevented execution, return `failed` with a clear explanation\n17\t\n18\tDo not use `needs_input` for transient infrastructure errors — those are `failed` and eligible for retry.\n19\t- Never modify files outside the scope of the task\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"5f48c5a5-0922-4aad-b478-4c94283d5513","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:40.286Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ae45bd19d2b74b1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n2\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n3\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n4\t\n5\tpackage prompts_test\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"testing\"\n9\t\t\"time\"\n10\t\n11\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n12\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n13\t\t\"github.com/onsi/gomega/format\"\n14\t)\n15\t\n16\tfunc TestSuite(t *testing.T) {\n17\t\ttime.Local = time.UTC\n18\t\tformat.TruncatedDiff = false\n19\t\tRegisterFailHandler(Fail)\n20\t\tsuiteConfig, reporterConfig := GinkgoConfiguration()\n21\t\tsuiteConfig.Timeout = 60 * time.Second\n22\t\tRunSpecs(t, \"Prompts Suite\", suiteConfig, reporterConfig)\n23\t}\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"8bd8cc0c-82ce-4358-b4fb-473570c454b6","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:40.288Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-975a66944db696e7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Definition of Done\n2\t\n3\tAfter completing your implementation, review your own changes against each criterion below. These are quality checks you perform by inspecting your work — not commands to run (linting and tests already ran via `validationCommand`). Report any unmet criterion as a blocker.\n4\t\n5\t## Code Quality\n6\t\n7\t- Exported types, functions, and interfaces have doc comments\n8\t- Error handling follows project conventions (no silently ignored errors)\n9\t- No debug output (print statements, fmt.Printf) — use structured logging\n10\t\n11\t## Testing\n12\t\n13\t- New code has good test coverage (target >= 80%)\n14\t- Changes to existing code have tests covering at least the changed behavior\n15\t\n16\t## Dependencies\n17\t\n18\t- If `make precommit` fails due to a dependency vulnerability with a known fix version, update the dependency (`go get <pkg>@<fixed-version> && go mod tidy && go mod vendor`) as part of your change\n19\t- No `exclude` or `replace` directives in go.mod (break remote install)\n20\t\n21\t## Documentation\n22\t\n23\t- README.md is updated if the change affects usage, configuration, or setup\n24\t- Documentation is updated if the change affects behavior described in docs/ (notably `docs/observation-scripts.md` and `docs/verdict-gate.md`)\n25\t- When changing CLI args, config fields, env vars, or flags (add, rename, remove, change default), grep the entire repo and update all references in docs/, README.md, examples, and comments\n26\t- CHANGELOG.md has an entry under `## Unreleased`\n27\t- New or changed integration seam (per the dark-factory scenario-writing rules, \"When to Write a Scenario\") → scenario under `scenarios/` added or updated\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"78d129b8-74cf-4874-a9c9-b465d2dd9805","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:40.289Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94ef948edb067886","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tYour final response MUST be a single JSON object with this schema:\n2\t\n3\t```json\n4\t{\n5\t  \"status\": \"done\" | \"failed\" | \"needs_input\",\n6\t  \"message\": \"human-readable summary of what happened\",\n7\t  \"files\": [\"list\", \"of\", \"files\", \"created-or-modified\"]\n8\t}\n9\t```\n10\t\n11\tField rules:\n12\t- `status`: required — `done` (success), `failed` (error), or `needs_input` (blocked on missing info)\n13\t- `message`: required — concise summary, one or two sentences\n14\t- `files`: optional — list of file paths created or modified during execution\n15\t\n16\tDo NOT wrap the JSON in markdown code fences. Output raw JSON only.\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"344bd839-e776-4b40-aa96-53d1defa0e42","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:40.291Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
