{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b1d893274e79da6f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n2\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n3\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n4\t\n5\t// Command defect-diagnoser-agent is the canonical AI-heavy agent: one Claude\n6\t// invocation per phase, all logic in the prompt + allowed tools.\n7\t//\n8\t// This binary is the Kafka entry point — spawned as a K8s Job by\n9\t// task/executor with TASK_CONTENT + TASK_ID + PHASE + KAFKA_BROKERS env.\n10\t// For local CLI mode (file-based), see cmd/run-task/main.go.\n11\t//\n12\t// Reference implementation for AI-heavy agents using the agent framework\n13\t// (lib.NewAgent + claude.NewAgentStep). Other agents (trade-analysis,\n14\t// pr-reviewer) follow the same shape — copy this main.go and swap\n15\t// prompts/tools.\n16\tpackage main\n17\t\n18\timport (\n19\t\t\"context\"\n20\t\t\"os\"\n21\t\t\"time\"\n22\t\n23\t\tagentlib \"github.com/bborbe/agent\"\n24\t\tclaudelib \"github.com/bborbe/agent/claude\"\n25\t\tdelivery \"github.com/bborbe/agent/delivery\"\n26\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/agent/envparse\"\n27\t\tlibmetrics \"github.com/bborbe/agent/metrics\"\n28\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/cqrs/base\"\n29\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/errors\"\n30\t\tlibkafka \"github.com/bborbe/kafka\"\n31\t\tlibsentry \"github.com/bborbe/sentry\"\n32\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/service\"\n33\t\tlibtime \"github.com/bborbe/time\"\n34\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/vault-cli/pkg/domain\"\n35\t\t\"github.com/golang/glog\"\n36\t\t\"github.com/prometheus/client_golang/prometheus\"\n37\t\t\"github.com/prometheus/client_golang/prometheus/push\"\n38\t\n39\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/factory\"\n40\t)\n41\t\n42\t// agentName is the identity string used for Prometheus metric grouping and logging.\n43\tconst agentName = \"claude-agent\"\n44\t\n45\tfunc main() {\n46\t\tapp := &application{}\n47\t\tos.Exit(service.Main(context.Background(), app, &app.SentryDSN, &app.SentryProxy))\n48\t}\n49\t\n50\ttype application struct {\n51\t\tSentryDSN   string `required:\"false\" arg:\"sentry-dsn\"   env:\"SENTRY_DSN\"   usage:\"SentryDSN\"    display:\"length\"`\n52\t\tSentryProxy string `required:\"false\" arg:\"sentry-proxy\" env:\"SENTRY_PROXY\" usage:\"Sentry Proxy\" display:\"length\"`\n53\t\n54\t\t// Claude Code CLI configuration\n55\t\tClaudeConfigDir claudelib.ClaudeConfigDir `required:\"false\" arg:\"claude-config-dir\" env:\"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\" usage:\"Claude Code config directory\"`\n56\t\n57\t\t// Agent directory (contains .claude/ with CLAUDE.md and commands)\n58\t\tAgentDir claudelib.AgentDir `required:\"false\" arg:\"agent-dir\" env:\"AGENT_DIR\" usage:\"Agent directory with .claude/ config\" default:\"agent\"`\n59\t\n60\t\t// Allowed tools (comma-separated)\n61\t\tAllowedToolsRaw string `required:\"false\" arg:\"allowed-tools\" env:\"ALLOWED_TOOLS\" usage:\"Comma-separated list of allowed tools\"`\n62\t\n63\t\t// Task content from agent pipeline\n64\t\tTaskContent string `required:\"true\" arg:\"task-content\" env:\"TASK_CONTENT\" usage:\"Raw task markdown from vault\"`\n65\t\n66\t\t// Environment context passed to prompt (comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs)\n67\t\tEnvContextRaw string `required:\"false\" arg:\"env-context\" env:\"ENV_CONTEXT\" usage:\"Comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs for prompt context\"`\n68\t\n69\t\t// Environment variables passed to Claude CLI process (comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs).\n70\t\t// Use this for ad-hoc / less-common env vars. The three load-bearing Anthropic provider\n71\t\t// vars below have dedicated arg slots so they don't have to be packed into this string.\n72\t\tClaudeEnvRaw string `required:\"false\" arg:\"claude-env\" env:\"CLAUDE_ENV\" usage:\"Comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs for Claude CLI environment\"`\n73\t\n74\t\t// Anthropic-compatible provider routing. Setting AnthropicBaseURL + AnthropicAuthToken\n75\t\t// routes the claude CLI to an alt-provider (e.g. MiniMax via https://api.minimax.io/anthropic).\n76\t\t// AnthropicModel drives both the `--model` CLI flag and the ANTHROPIC_MODEL env var seen by\n77\t\t// the claude subprocess. Non-empty values override the same keys in ClaudeEnvRaw.\n78\t\tAnthropicBaseURL   string                `required:\"false\" arg:\"anthropic-base-url\"   env:\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\"   usage:\"Anthropic-compatible API base URL\"`\n79\t\tAnthropicAuthToken string                `required:\"false\" arg:\"anthropic-auth-token\" env:\"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\" usage:\"Bearer token for ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\"                                  display:\"password\"`\n80\t\tAnthropicModel     claudelib.ClaudeModel `required:\"false\" arg:\"anthropic-model\"      env:\"ANTHROPIC_MODEL\"      usage:\"Model name; also exposed to the claude subprocess as ANTHROPIC_MODEL\"                    default:\"sonnet\"`\n81\t\n82\t\t// Branch for Kafka result delivery\n83\t\tBranch base.Branch `required:\"false\" arg:\"branch\" env:\"BRANCH\" usage:\"branch\"`\n84\t\n85\t\t// TopicPrefix is an explicit Kafka topic prefix, independent of Branch.\n86\t\tTopicPrefix base.TopicPrefix `required:\"false\" arg:\"topic-prefix\" env:\"TOPIC_PREFIX\" usage:\"Explicit Kafka topic prefix; empty means unprefixed topics\"`\n87\t\n88\t\t// Phase to run (framework requires explicit phase)\n89\t\tPhase domain.TaskPhase `required:\"false\" arg:\"phase\" env:\"PHASE\" usage:\"Agent phase: planning | execution | ai_review\" default:\"execution\"`\n90\t\n91\t\t// Kafka delivery (optional — only active when TASK_ID is set)\n92\t\tKafkaBrokers libkafka.Brokers        `required:\"false\" arg:\"kafka-brokers\" env:\"KAFKA_BROKERS\" usage:\"Comma separated list of Kafka brokers\"`\n93\t\tTaskID       agentlib.TaskIdentifier `required:\"false\" arg:\"task-id\"       env:\"TASK_ID\"       usage:\"Agent task identifier for publishing results back to task controller\"`\n94\t\n95\t\tPushgatewayURL string `required:\"false\" arg:\"pushgateway-url\" env:\"PUSHGATEWAY_URL\" usage:\"Prometheus PushGateway URL\"          default:\"http://pushgateway:9090\"`\n96\t\tTaskType       string `required:\"false\" arg:\"task-type\"       env:\"TASK_TYPE\"       usage:\"Task type label for metric grouping\" default:\"unknown\"`\n97\t}\n98\t\n99\tfunc (a *application) Run(ctx context.Context, _ libsentry.Client) error {\n100\t\tregistry := prometheus.NewRegistry()\n101\t\tjobMetrics := libmetrics.NewJobMetrics(registry, libtime.NewCurrentDateTime())\n102\t\tpusher := push.New(a.PushgatewayURL, libmetrics.BuildJobMetricsName(agentName)).\n103\t\t\tGrouping(\"agent\", agentName).\n104\t\t\tGrouping(\"task_type\", a.TaskType).\n105\t\t\tCollector(registry)\n106\t\tdefer func() {\n107\t\t\tif err := pusher.PushContext(ctx); err != nil {\n108\t\t\t\tglog.Warningf(\"prometheus push failed: %v\", err)\n109\t\t\t\treturn\n110\t\t\t}\n111\t\t\tglog.V(2).Infof(\"prometheus push completed\")\n112\t\t}()\n113\t\tstart := libtime.NewCurrentDateTime().Now().Time()\n114\t\n115\t\tglog.V(2).Infof(\"defect-diagnoser-agent started phase=%s\", a.Phase)\n116\t\n117\t\tdeliverer := delivery.NewNoopResultDeliverer()\n118\t\tif a.TaskID != \"\" {\n119\t\t\tif len(a.KafkaBrokers) == 0 {\n120\t\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n121\t\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n122\t\t\t\treturn errors.Errorf(ctx, \"KAFKA_BROKERS must be set when TASK_ID is set\")\n123\t\t\t}\n124\t\t\tsyncProducer, err := factory.CreateSyncProducer(ctx, a.KafkaBrokers)\n125\t\t\tif err != nil {\n126\t\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n127\t\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n128\t\t\t\treturn errors.Wrap(ctx, err, \"create sync producer\")\n129\t\t\t}\n130\t\t\tdefer func() {\n131\t\t\t\tif err := syncProducer.Close(); err != nil {\n132\t\t\t\t\tglog.Warningf(\"close sync producer failed: %v\", err)\n133\t\t\t\t}\n134\t\t\t}()\n135\t\t\tdeliverer = factory.CreateKafkaResultDeliverer(\n136\t\t\t\tsyncProducer, a.TopicPrefix, a.TaskID, a.TaskContent,\n137\t\t\t\tlibtime.NewCurrentDateTime(),\n138\t\t\t)\n139\t\t}\n140\t\n141\t\tclaudeEnv := envparse.KeyValuePairs(a.ClaudeEnvRaw)\n142\t\tif claudeEnv == nil {\n143\t\t\tclaudeEnv = map[string]string{}\n144\t\t}\n145\t\tif a.AnthropicBaseURL != \"\" {\n146\t\t\tclaudeEnv[\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\"] = a.AnthropicBaseURL\n147\t\t}\n148\t\tif a.AnthropicAuthToken != \"\" {\n149\t\t\tclaudeEnv[\"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\"] = a.AnthropicAuthToken\n150\t\t}\n151\t\tif a.AnthropicModel != \"\" {\n152\t\t\tclaudeEnv[\"ANTHROPIC_MODEL\"] = a.AnthropicModel.String()\n153\t\t}\n154\t\n155\t\tprovider := factory.CreateAgentProvider(\n156\t\t\ta.ClaudeConfigDir,\n157\t\t\ta.AgentDir,\n158\t\t\tclaudelib.ParseAllowedTools(a.AllowedToolsRaw),\n159\t\t\ta.AnthropicModel,\n160\t\t\tclaudeEnv,\n161\t\t\tenvparse.KeyValuePairs(a.EnvContextRaw),\n162\t\t)\n163\t\tagent, err := provider.Get(ctx, agentlib.TaskType(a.TaskType))\n164\t\tif err != nil {\n165\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n166\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n167\t\t\treturn errors.Wrap(ctx, err, \"select agent for task_type\")\n168\t\t}\n169\t\n170\t\tresult, err := agent.Run(ctx, a.Phase, a.TaskContent, deliverer)\n171\t\tif err != nil {\n172\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(agentlib.AgentStatusFailed)\n173\t\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n174\t\t\treturn errors.Wrap(ctx, err, \"agent run failed\")\n175\t\t}\n176\t\tjobMetrics.RecordRun(result.Status)\n177\t\tjobMetrics.RecordDuration(time.Since(start))\n178\t\treturn agentlib.PrintResult(ctx, result)\n179\t}\n180\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"3c6aed61-05ca-4001-85ca-62eab67e8be1","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:43.544Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eb53f59b143d113","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tinclude tools.env\n2\t\n3\tdefault: precommit\n4\t\n5\tprecommit: ensure format generate test check addlicense\n6\t\t@echo \"ready to commit\"\n7\t\n8\tensure:\n9\t\tgo mod tidy\n10\t\tgo mod verify\n11\t\trm -rf vendor\n12\t\n13\tformat:\n14\t\tfind . -type f -name 'go.mod' -not -path './vendor/*' -exec go run github.com/shoenig/go-modtool@$(GO_MODTOOL_VERSION) -w fmt \"{}\" \\;\n15\t\tgo run github.com/incu6us/goimports-reviser/v3@$(GOIMPORTS_REVISER_VERSION) -project-name github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent -format -excludes vendor ./...\n16\t\tfind . -type d -name vendor -prune -o -type f -name '*.go' -print0 | xargs -0 -n 10 go run github.com/segmentio/golines@$(GOLINES_VERSION) --max-len=100 -w\n17\t\tfind . -type f -name '*.go' -not -path './vendor/*' -exec gofmt -w \"{}\" +\n18\t\n19\tgenerate:\n20\t\trm -rf mocks avro\n21\t\tmkdir -p mocks\n22\t\techo \"package mocks\" > mocks/mocks.go\n23\t\tgo generate -mod=mod ./...\n24\t\n25\t.PHONY: generatek8s\n26\tgeneratek8s:\n27\t\tbash hack/update-codegen.sh\n28\t\n29\t# -race=true catches data races but flakes on some CI runners (rare SIGSEGV\n30\t# during gexec.Build in cmd/*-style binary smoke tests). Default off; opt in\n31\t# via ENABLE_RACE=true for nightly/manual hardening runs.\n32\tTESTFLAGS_RACE = -race=false\n33\tifdef ENABLE_RACE\n34\t\tTESTFLAGS_RACE = -race=true\n35\tendif\n36\t\n37\t.PHONY: test\n38\ttest:\n39\t\tgo test -mod=mod -p=$${GO_TEST_PARALLEL:-1} -cover $(TESTFLAGS_RACE) $(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/)\n40\t\n41\tcheck: lint vet errcheck vulncheck osv-scanner gosec trivy\n42\t\n43\tlint:\n44\t\tgo run github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@$(GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION) run --allow-parallel-runners --config .golangci.yml ./...\n45\t\n46\tvet:\n47\t\tgo vet -mod=mod $(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/)\n48\t\n49\terrcheck:\n50\t\tGODEBUG=gotypesalias=1 go run github.com/kisielk/errcheck@$(ERRCHECK_VERSION) -ignore '(Close|Write|Fprint)' $(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/ | grep -v k8s/client)\n51\t\n52\tVULNCHECK_IGNORE ?= GO-2026-4923 GO-2026-4514 GO-2022-0470 GO-2026-4772 GO-2026-4771 GO-2026-5932 GO-2026-5064 GO-2026-5338 GO-2026-5622\n53\t\n54\t.PHONY: vulncheck\n55\tvulncheck:\n56\t\t@PKGS=\"$(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/)\"; \\\n57\t\tIGNORE_JSON=$$(printf '%s\\n' $(VULNCHECK_IGNORE) | jq -R . | jq -s .); \\\n58\t\tREMAIN=$$(go run golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@$(GOVULNCHECK_VERSION) -format json $$PKGS 2>/dev/null | \\\n59\t\t\tjq -rs --argjson ignore \"$$IGNORE_JSON\" \\\n60\t\t\t\t'(map(select(.osv != null)) | map({key: .osv.id, value: (.osv.summary // \"\")}) | from_entries) as $$sum | \\\n61\t\t\t\t map(select(.finding != null) | .finding) | \\\n62\t\t\t\t map(select(.osv as $$o | $$ignore | index($$o) | not)) | \\\n63\t\t\t\t map(\"\\(.osv)\\t\\(.trace[-1].module)@\\(.trace[-1].version) -> \\(.fixed_version)\\t\\($$sum[.osv] // \"\")\") | \\\n64\t\t\t\t unique | .[]'); \\\n65\t\tif [ -n \"$$REMAIN\" ]; then \\\n66\t\t\techo \"Unexpected vulnerabilities (ignored: $(VULNCHECK_IGNORE)):\"; \\\n67\t\t\tprintf '%s\\n' \"$$REMAIN\" | column -t -s \"$$(printf '\\t')\"; \\\n68\t\t\texit 1; \\\n69\t\telse \\\n70\t\t\techo \"No unignored vulnerabilities found\"; \\\n71\t\tfi\n72\t\n73\tosv-scanner:\n74\t\t@if [ -f .osv-scanner.toml ]; then \\\n75\t\t\techo \"Using .osv-scanner.toml\"; \\\n76\t\t\tgo run github.com/google/osv-scanner/v2/cmd/osv-scanner@$(OSV_SCANNER_VERSION) --config .osv-scanner.toml --recursive .; \\\n77\t\telse \\\n78\t\t\techo \"No config found, running default scan\"; \\\n79\t\t\tgo run github.com/google/osv-scanner/v2/cmd/osv-scanner@$(OSV_SCANNER_VERSION) --recursive .; \\\n80\t\tfi\n81\t\n82\tgosec:\n83\t\tgo run github.com/securego/gosec/v2/cmd/gosec@$(GOSEC_VERSION) -exclude=G104 ./...\n84\t\n85\t.PHONY: trivy\n86\ttrivy:\n87\t\ttrivy fs \\\n88\t\t--db-repository ghcr.io/aquasecurity/trivy-db \\\n89\t\t$(if $(wildcard .trivyignore),--ignorefile .trivyignore,$(if $(wildcard $(ROOTDIR)/.trivyignore),--ignorefile $(ROOTDIR)/.trivyignore,)) \\\n90\t\t$(if $(wildcard .trivy-secret.yaml),--secret-config .trivy-secret.yaml,$(if $(wildcard $(ROOTDIR)/.trivy-secret.yaml),--secret-config $(ROOTDIR)/.trivy-secret.yaml,)) \\\n91\t\t--scanners vuln,secret \\\n92\t\t--skip-dirs vendor \\\n93\t\t--quiet \\\n94\t\t--no-progress \\\n95\t\t--disable-telemetry \\\n96\t\t--exit-code 1 .\n97\t\n98\taddlicense:\n99\t\tgo run github.com/google/addlicense@$(ADDLICENSE_VERSION) -c \"Benjamin Borbe\" -y $$(date +'%Y') -l bsd $$(find . -name \"*.go\" -not -path './vendor/*')\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"d4db38c8-6d95-4c2d-a2ec-534a783d65f8","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:43.549Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fc72114f0200420","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n2\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n3\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n4\t\n5\t// Command run-task is the local-CLI entry point for defect-diagnoser-agent.\n6\t//\n7\t// Reads a markdown task file from disk, runs the agent against it, and\n8\t// writes the updated content back to the same file. Mirrors the Kafka\n9\t// entry point (../../main.go) but uses file I/O instead of Kafka/CQRS.\n10\t//\n11\t// Used for local development and integration testing without spinning up\n12\t// a K8s Job + Kafka cluster.\n13\tpackage main\n14\t\n15\timport (\n16\t\t\"context\"\n17\t\t\"os\"\n18\t\n19\t\tagentlib \"github.com/bborbe/agent\"\n20\t\tclaudelib \"github.com/bborbe/agent/claude\"\n21\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/agent/envparse\"\n22\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/cqrs/base\"\n23\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/errors\"\n24\t\tlibsentry \"github.com/bborbe/sentry\"\n25\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/service\"\n26\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/vault-cli/pkg/domain\"\n27\t\n28\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/factory\"\n29\t)\n30\t\n31\tfunc main() {\n32\t\tapp := &application{}\n33\t\tos.Exit(service.Main(context.Background(), app, &app.SentryDSN, &app.SentryProxy))\n34\t}\n35\t\n36\ttype application struct {\n37\t\tSentryDSN   string `required:\"false\" arg:\"sentry-dsn\"   env:\"SENTRY_DSN\"   usage:\"SentryDSN\"    display:\"length\"`\n38\t\tSentryProxy string `required:\"false\" arg:\"sentry-proxy\" env:\"SENTRY_PROXY\" usage:\"Sentry Proxy\" display:\"length\"`\n39\t\n40\t\t// Claude Code CLI configuration\n41\t\tClaudeConfigDir claudelib.ClaudeConfigDir `required:\"false\" arg:\"claude-config-dir\" env:\"CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR\" usage:\"Claude Code config directory\"`\n42\t\n43\t\t// Agent directory (contains .claude/ with CLAUDE.md and commands)\n44\t\tAgentDir claudelib.AgentDir `required:\"false\" arg:\"agent-dir\" env:\"AGENT_DIR\" usage:\"Agent directory with .claude/ config\" default:\"agent\"`\n45\t\n46\t\t// Allowed tools (comma-separated)\n47\t\tAllowedToolsRaw string `required:\"false\" arg:\"allowed-tools\" env:\"ALLOWED_TOOLS\" usage:\"Comma-separated list of allowed tools\"`\n48\t\n49\t\t// Environment context passed to prompt (comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs)\n50\t\tEnvContextRaw string `required:\"false\" arg:\"env-context\" env:\"ENV_CONTEXT\" usage:\"Comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs for prompt context\"`\n51\t\n52\t\t// Environment variables passed to Claude CLI process (comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs).\n53\t\t// Use this for ad-hoc / less-common env vars. The three load-bearing Anthropic provider\n54\t\t// vars below have dedicated arg slots so they don't have to be packed into this string.\n55\t\tClaudeEnvRaw string `required:\"false\" arg:\"claude-env\" env:\"CLAUDE_ENV\" usage:\"Comma-separated KEY=VALUE pairs for Claude CLI environment\"`\n56\t\n57\t\t// Anthropic-compatible provider routing. Setting AnthropicBaseURL + AnthropicAuthToken\n58\t\t// routes the claude CLI to an alt-provider (e.g. MiniMax via https://api.minimax.io/anthropic).\n59\t\t// AnthropicModel drives both the `--model` CLI flag and the ANTHROPIC_MODEL env var seen by\n60\t\t// the claude subprocess. Non-empty values override the same keys in ClaudeEnvRaw.\n61\t\tAnthropicBaseURL   string                `required:\"false\" arg:\"anthropic-base-url\"   env:\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\"   usage:\"Anthropic-compatible API base URL\"`\n62\t\tAnthropicAuthToken string                `required:\"false\" arg:\"anthropic-auth-token\" env:\"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\" usage:\"Bearer token for ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\"                                  display:\"password\"`\n63\t\tAnthropicModel     claudelib.ClaudeModel `required:\"false\" arg:\"anthropic-model\"      env:\"ANTHROPIC_MODEL\"      usage:\"Model name; also exposed to the claude subprocess as ANTHROPIC_MODEL\"                    default:\"sonnet\"`\n64\t\n65\t\t// Environment\n66\t\tBranch base.Branch `required:\"true\" arg:\"branch\" env:\"BRANCH\" usage:\"branch\" default:\"dev\"`\n67\t\n68\t\t// Phase to run (defaults to execution; framework requires explicit phase)\n69\t\tPhase domain.TaskPhase `required:\"false\" arg:\"phase\" env:\"PHASE\" usage:\"Agent phase: planning | execution | ai_review\" default:\"execution\"`\n70\t\n71\t\t// Task file for local development\n72\t\tTaskFilePath string `required:\"true\" arg:\"task-file\" env:\"TASK_FILE\" usage:\"Path to the markdown task file\"`\n73\t}\n74\t\n75\tfunc (a *application) Run(ctx context.Context, _ libsentry.Client) error {\n76\t\ttaskContent, err := os.ReadFile(\n77\t\t\ta.TaskFilePath,\n78\t\t) // #nosec G304 -- filePath from trusted CLI input\n79\t\tif err != nil {\n80\t\t\treturn errors.Wrap(ctx, err, \"read task file: \"+a.TaskFilePath)\n81\t\t}\n82\t\n83\t\tdeliverer := factory.CreateFileResultDeliverer(a.TaskFilePath)\n84\t\n85\t\tclaudeEnv := envparse.KeyValuePairs(a.ClaudeEnvRaw)\n86\t\tif claudeEnv == nil {\n87\t\t\tclaudeEnv = map[string]string{}\n88\t\t}\n89\t\tif a.AnthropicBaseURL != \"\" {\n90\t\t\tclaudeEnv[\"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\"] = a.AnthropicBaseURL\n91\t\t}\n92\t\tif a.AnthropicAuthToken != \"\" {\n93\t\t\tclaudeEnv[\"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\"] = a.AnthropicAuthToken\n94\t\t}\n95\t\tif a.AnthropicModel != \"\" {\n96\t\t\tclaudeEnv[\"ANTHROPIC_MODEL\"] = a.AnthropicModel.String()\n97\t\t}\n98\t\n99\t\tagent := factory.CreateAgent(\n100\t\t\ta.ClaudeConfigDir,\n101\t\t\ta.AgentDir,\n102\t\t\tclaudelib.ParseAllowedTools(a.AllowedToolsRaw),\n103\t\t\ta.AnthropicModel,\n104\t\t\tclaudeEnv,\n105\t\t\tenvparse.KeyValuePairs(a.EnvContextRaw),\n106\t\t)\n107\t\n108\t\tresult, err := agent.Run(ctx, a.Phase, string(taskContent), deliverer)\n109\t\tif err != nil {\n110\t\t\treturn errors.Wrap(ctx, err, \"agent run failed\")\n111\t\t}\n112\t\treturn agentlib.PrintResult(ctx, result)\n113\t}\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"38b9084c-b028-47f0-a5a6-5537fbeb7f1c","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:43.554Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbff6bfeafafc34e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tinclude Makefile.variables\n2\tinclude Makefile.precommit\n3\tinclude Makefile.docker\n4\t\n5\tDOCKER_REGISTRY ?= docker.io\n6\tIMAGE ?= bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent\n7\tifeq ($(VERSION),)\n8\t\tVERSION := $(shell git describe --tags `git rev-list --tags --max-count=1`)\n9\tendif\n10\t\n11\t# Local dev only. Runtime config (kafka brokers, sentry DSN, stage vars) and the\n12\t# full deployment moved to the quant config repo — this is now a publish-only\n13\t# source repo (see CHANGELOG). Pass any flags/env locally as needed.\n14\trun:\n15\t\t@go run -mod=mod main.go -v=2\n16\t\n17\tdeps:\n18\t\tgo install github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2/ginkgo@v2.25.3\n19\t\tsudo port install trivy\n20\t\n21\t.PHONY: fix\n22\tfix:\n23\t\t@for dir in $$(find `pwd` -type d -name vendor -prune -o -name go.mod -exec dirname \"{}\" \\; | grep -v '^$$'); do \\\n24\t\t\tcd $${dir}; \\\n25\t\t\techo \"fix $${dir}\"; \\\n26\t\t\tgo get \\\n27\t\t\tgithub.com/bborbe/kv@latest \\\n28\t\t\tgithub.com/bborbe/memorykv@latest \\\n29\t\t\tgithub.com/bborbe/badgerkv@latest \\\n30\t\t\tgithub.com/bborbe/boltkv@latest \\\n31\t\t\tgithub.com/go-git/go-git/v5@latest \\\n32\t\t\tgithub.com/containerd/containerd@latest \\\n33\t\t\tgolang.org/x/crypto@latest \\\n34\t\t\tgolang.org/x/net@latest; \\\n35\t\tdone\n36\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"140b6930-c1c3-4c45-84aa-b33370ba713b","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:27:43.558Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts from spec 001"}
