{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaddbf37827b8ecc","type":"tool_result","content":"2026-09-27T22:34:42Z\n--- grep pod in repo docs/prose ---\n/workspace/agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md:15:- **Observe the running system only through the read-only scripts in `scripts/`** (task files, Prometheus, pod logs/events). They are the sole exception to the internal-network rule below, and only as scripts — never reach a cluster address directly.\n/workspace/README.md:7:- **Observes (read-only, in order):** task files → Prometheus → pod logs/events via its own read-only service account\n/workspace/k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:41:    ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/pod-logs.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"\n/workspace/k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:54:  # Pod logs/events (read path 3) need a dedicated read-only ServiceAccount `defect-diagnoser`\n--- readme lines with pod ---\n7:- **Observes (read-only, in order):** task files → Prometheus → pod logs/events via its own read-only service account\n47:The `Config` CRD's `spec.env` map becomes pod env vars, which `main.go` consumes via struct tags. Example from `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`:\n68:`lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) before spawning `claude`. Custom env vars (API URLs, credentials) **must** be threaded explicitly via `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env map[string]string` in `main.go`. Don't expect pod env to reach Claude by default. See `docs/` for precedent (trade-analysis commit `1ccfa674cf`).\n--- CLAUDE_ENV in readme ---\n32:| `CLAUDE_ENV` | no | — | Comma-separated `KEY=VAL` pairs passed to the Claude CLI subprocess |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"d416bb13-2da2-425f-b44b-c18d60239941",