{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"abb63d3bf6d518747","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94115c2446396ba4","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace/31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933/tasks/abb63d3bf6d518747.output","summary":"All three prompts are written and every verification command in them has been executed against a faithful scratch implementation.\n\n## Files created\n\n- `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md`\n- `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-repo-clone-script.md`\n- `/workspace/prompts/3-spec-001-config-allowlist-and-consistency.md`\n\nExecution order: `1` → `2` → `3` (filename prefixes; prompts 1 and 2 are independent leaves, 3 depends on both). All three carry `spec: [\"001-read-only-observation-toolkit\"]` and only the `spec`/`status`/`created` frontmatter fields.\n\n## Decomposition\n\nI kept the spec's own 3-prompt split unchanged — it survives the grouping and verifiability tests, and folding the consistency test into prompt 3 is correct because AC8 needs all four scripts on disk *and* the allowlist updated in the same change. Three deviations from the spec, each deliberate:\n\n1. **`.gitignore` moved from prompt 3 into prompt 2** (prompt 3 keeps an idempotent \"exactly one occurrence\" check). Prompt 2's tests create real clone trees under `<repo>/agent/repos/`; with the ignore line arriving only in prompt 3, a test run killed mid-spec would leave a nested clone for dark-factory to commit. AC11 still holds after all three prompts.\n2. **Test location decided**: a test-only package `pkg/scripts/` (`package scripts_test` only). I verified empirically that a directory with only external-test files compiles and runs under `go test ./...`, and told both prompts not to \"fix\" it with a non-test file.\n3. **Suite-file ownership**: prompt 1 creates `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` (with `repoRoot()`); prompt 2 embeds byte-identical content behind an \"if absent, create; if present, leave\" guard; prompt 3 references it (it depends on 1 and 2). Two `RunSpecs` in one package fail the build, so this had to be pinned. The embedded Go block hashes identically across prompts 1 and 2.\n\n## Two defects found in the spec's own acceptance commands\n\n- **AC8's exact-string check cannot pass as written.** The spec says `grep -c 'ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"…Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*)…\"'` prints `1`. Plain `grep` is BRE, where `*` is a quantifier, so `:*)` compiles to \"zero-or-more `:` then `)`\" and never matches the literal `:*`. I ran it: it returns **0**. Prompt 3 uses `grep -cF` (verified to return 1) and documents the substitution in an HTML comment. The consistency test itself compares captured strings, never a shell pattern.\n- **AC7/AC11 spell leading whitespace `\\s`** (a GNU extension). Prompt 3 uses `[[:space:]]`, same assertion, portable; noted in the same comment.\n\n## Empirical verification performed (not just written)\n\nI built a recording HTTP server, a stub `git`, a candidate set of scripts, and a scratch copy of the repo with the intended edits applied, then ran every command from the prompts' `<verification>` blocks verbatim:\n\n- AC4 → `1` per file; AC9 curl pipeline → `0`; AC10 → no matches; executability checks pass.\n- Behaviour: 500/401 → exit 1 with the status on stderr; 100 KiB → exactly 65536 stdout bytes + `truncated` + exit 0; `25 Tasks/x y.md` → raw path `/api/v1/files/25%20Tasks/x%20y.md`; all 11 AC5 rejections → exit 2, zero stub-git invocations, identical snapshots; symlink escape → rejected with the sentinel intact; second clone → 2 `clone` invocations, marker-1 gone / marker-2 present, `find -perm -u+w` empty; 128 → `git clone failed`.\n- AC7 (all four), AC8 (both), AC11 (all eleven) → pass against the scratch copy.\n\n## Environment hazard worth a global rule\n\nThe container sets `http_proxy`/`HTTPS_PROXY` and no `NO_PROXY`. `curl` honours them, so a loopback request to the test server is sent to the proxy (I got `403` and an empty server log) — which silently **inverts** every \"zero requests\" assertion. Both prompts therefore require the child env to be built explicitly (`PATH` + `HOME` in a temp dir + only the variable under test), never `os.Environ()`. This belongs in `~/.claude-yolo/CLAUDE.md` — it affects any prompt whose tests make loopback HTTP calls.\n\n## Open questions / residual risks surfaced\n\n- `envparse.KeyValuePairs` could **not** be grep-verified: `/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/` is empty here. Mitigated by pointing prompt 3 at the in-repo call sites (`main.go`, `cmd/run-task/main.go`) and requiring the executor to read that line before writing the test.\n- `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer` is not reachable from this container. Prompt 2 says so explicitly and forbids guessing or copying from it.\n- Prompt 3 requirement 7h adds a small `envparse.KeyValuePairs` assertion beyond AC7's greps. Justification is in the requirement: it is the only container-side guard for the seam AC12 proves operator-side (a value that greps correctly but parses into one key would otherwise ship). Flagged here for the reviewer in case you want it dropped as scope.\n- AC12 is stated in prompt 3 as a negative constraint (operator-side, not reproducible here), not as an operator-procedure block.\n\n## Docs referenced in `<context>` (in-container paths)\n\n`/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md`; `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/` → `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md`, `go-security-linting.md`, `changelog-guide.md`; project `docs/observation-scripts.md`, `docs/dod.md`. No scenario prompt was emitted: the spec says \"no new scenario\", and all four scenario-writing conditions fail (script tests with a recording server and a stub `git` reach every behaviour; scenario 001 covers the live journey).\n\n## Patterns inlined because no doc covers them\n\n1. Test-only Go package that shells out to repo scripts + walks up to `go.mod` for the repo root — suggest a section in `go-testing-guide.md`.\n2. The bash \"capture `curl` status with `-w '%{http_code}'` + cap stdout at N bytes without SIGPIPE\" recipe (pipe-to-`head` is the trap) — no doc exists; suggest `bash-read-only-http-script-pattern.md`.\n3. Stub-binary-on-`PATH` testing with a per-call marker file — suggest `go-testing-guide.md`.\n\nSuggested next step: run `/audit-prompt` on each file before approving.","usage":{"total_tokens":176737,"tool_uses":66,"duration_ms":874405},"uuid":"12b2017f-348c-4cd4-923c-3e698a220128","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933"}
