{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b60078ddbb64bc34","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: generating\n3\tapproved: \"2026-09-27T22:26:16Z\"\n4\tgenerating: \"2026-09-27T22:27:05Z\"\n5\tbranch: dark-factory/read-only-observation-toolkit\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Summary\n9\t\n10\t- Give the defect diagnoser its four read-only \"eyes\" on the running system: two scripts that read task files from the vault, one that queries Prometheus, and one that makes a read-only clone of a source repo.\n11\t- Make the vault and Prometheus addresses actually reach the model. Today they sit in the Config as plain pod env, which the runner silently strips; the fix routes them through the existing `CLAUDE_ENV` passthrough instead of new code.\n12\t- Line up the Config's tool allowlist, the container image, the guardrails and the README with what really exists, and drop the pod-log tool, which cannot work on the current platform.\n13\t- This spec adds no diagnosis logic. It is the foundation that spec `diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate` builds on.\n14\t\n15\t## Problem\n16\t\n17\tThe scaffolded `defect-diagnoser-agent` Config allowlists five scripts, and none of them exists. One (`pod-logs.sh`) cannot work at all, because the Config CRD has no `serviceAccountName` field and an agent Job therefore has no Kubernetes read access.\n18\t\n19\tThe Config sets `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` as plain pod env. The Claude runner passes only a fixed allowlist of pod variables into the model's subprocess, so even correct scripts would fail with \"variable is required\" while `kubectl describe pod` shows the variable set.\n20\t\n21\tThe image does not install `git`, so no clone can work. And the only existing clone script (in `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer`) accepts `..` as an owner or repo name. A crafted reference therefore escapes the clone directory before the script runs `rm -rf` and `chmod -R`.\n22\t\n23\tWithout a safe, tested toolkit, the diagnoser either cannot observe anything or observes through tools that can be steered into writing or deleting.\n24\t\n25\t## Goal\n26\t\n27\tThe agent image carries four executable read-only scripts in `agent/scripts/`, each behaving exactly as `docs/observation-scripts.md` specifies. No script can send anything but a GET or write outside its own clone directory. Invalid arguments are rejected before any network call, `git` invocation or filesystem change, and HTTP failures surface their status.\n28\t\n29\tThe Config delivers `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` to the Claude subprocess through `CLAUDE_ENV`. The allowlist, the scripts on disk, and the prompt and guardrail prose agree in every direction. A test enforces that agreement, so an allowlisted script that does not exist, or a script that is not allowlisted, fails `make test`.\n30\t\n31\t## Non-goals\n32\t\n33\t- No pod-log / event reads or script. They wait on the Config CRD gaining a service-account field (NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2).\n34\t- No diagnosis prompts, task-type dispatch or verdict validation. Those belong to spec `diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate`, which depends on this one.\n35\t- No new Go env plumbing, flags or helper for the two URLs. The existing `CLAUDE_ENV` passthrough carries them.\n36\t- No private-repo clone auth (`GIT_CLONE_TOKEN` / GitHub App). v1 clones only repos reachable without credentials.\n37\t- No git-rest gateway auth (`GATEWAY_SECRET`).\n38\t- No Prometheus range queries, and no Prometheus path other than `/api/v1/query`.\n39\t- No `repo-clone.sh log` subcommand. Nothing in v1 consumes regression history.\n40\t- No `kubectl apply`, deploy, secret manifest or RBAC. The Config file stays NOT APPLIED.\n41\t- No change to the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module.\n42\t- Do NOT add a clone-directory, clone-depth, timeout or output-cap env knob. These are invariants; if a future consumer demands variation, that is a separate spec.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\tContainer-executable. Every test named below runs under `make test`. Script tests run as a non-root user. On uid 0 they skip the permission-restoration assertion, with a skip message naming that blind spot (root removes read-only trees without restoring permissions). Mode-bit assertions hold under any uid.\n47\t\n48\t- [ ] **AC1** `make precommit` exits 0 at the repo root. Evidence: exit code.\n49\t- [ ] **AC2** `prometheus-query.sh`, run against a recording HTTP test server:\n50\t  - One PromQL argument sends exactly one `GET` to path `/api/v1/query` whose `query` parameter equals the argument. The response body goes to stdout and the exit code is 0.\n51\t  - An argument starting with `/`, or containing `://`, exits 2 and the server receives zero requests.\n52\t  - Zero arguments, or two or more, exit non-zero with zero requests.\n53\t  - With `PROMETHEUS_URL` unset, it exits non-zero and stderr contains `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n54\t  - A `500` response exits non-zero with `500` on stderr; a `401` response exits non-zero with `401` on stderr.\n55\t  - A 100 KiB body produces exactly 65536 bytes on stdout, `truncated` on stderr, and exit 0.\n56\t\n57\t  Evidence: exit codes, recorded requests (method, path, query) and byte counts, asserted in tests.\n58\t- [ ] **AC3** `vault-read.sh` and `vault-list.sh`, run against a recording HTTP test server:\n59\t  - Every request either script sends is a `GET` under `/api/v1/files/`.\n60\t  - `vault-read.sh` rejects each of these with exit 2 and zero requests: `/etc/passwd`, `../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..`, `a.md?x=1`, `a.md#x`, `http://evil/x`.\n61\t  - `vault-read.sh \"25 Tasks/x y.md\"` requests the path with the space percent-encoded.\n62\t  - For **each** script: zero arguments, and two arguments, each exit non-zero with zero requests (contract: exactly one argument).\n63\t  - `vault-list.sh \"* Tasks/*.md\"` sends its argument as the `glob` query parameter.\n64\t  - For **each** script: with `GIT_REST_URL` unset, it exits non-zero and stderr contains `GIT_REST_URL`.\n65\t  - For **each** script: a `500` response and a `401` response each exit non-zero with the status on stderr.\n66\t  - For **each** script: a 100 KiB body produces exactly 65536 bytes on stdout, `truncated` on stderr, and exit 0.\n67\t\n68\t  Evidence: exit codes and recorded requests, asserted in tests.\n69\t- [ ] **AC4** Every HTTP script sets a 30 s timeout. `grep -c -- '--max-time 30' agent/scripts/vault-read.sh agent/scripts/vault-list.sh agent/scripts/prometheus-query.sh` prints a count of at least 1 for each file. Evidence: grep output.\n70\t- [ ] **AC5** `repo-clone.sh` rejects bad references. Setup: a stub `git` first on `PATH` logs every invocation, and a snapshot of path + mode bits for everything outside `<agent dir>/repos/` is taken before and after each case.\n71\t  - Each of these exits 2: `evil`, `a;b/c`, `http://evil.example/x/y`, `file:///etc/x`, `../x`, `x/..`, `x/.`, `./.`, `../..`, `https://github.com/../x`, `git@github.com:x/...git`.\n72\t  - So does `clone evil/x` when `<agent dir>/repos/evil` is a pre-planted symlink to a directory outside `repos/` (the defense-in-depth resolve check).\n73\t  - Every rejection leaves zero stub-git invocations and identical before/after snapshots.\n74\t\n75\t  Evidence: exit codes, an empty invocation log, and identical snapshots, asserted in tests.\n76\t- [ ] **AC6** `repo-clone.sh` success and error paths, with the stub `git`:\n77\t  - `clone bborbe/foo` produces exactly one `clone` invocation: `git clone https://github.com/bborbe/foo <agent dir>/repos/bborbe/foo`, with no `--recurse-submodules`. Stdout has an absolute `clone_path=` inside `<agent dir>/repos/`, plus `head_sha=` and `default_branch=` lines. `find <clone> -perm -u+w` prints nothing.\n78\t  - `clone bborbe/.github` is accepted, with exactly one `clone` invocation.\n79\t  - A second `clone bborbe/foo` exits 0. The stub log then shows 2 `clone` invocations, and the stub's first-call marker file is gone (only the second-call marker remains).\n80\t  - A stub `git clone` that exits 128 makes the script exit non-zero, with `git clone failed` on stderr.\n81\t  - `log x y` exits 2 with usage on stderr.\n82\t\n83\t  Evidence: exit codes, invocation log, marker files and `find` output, asserted in tests.\n84\t- [ ] **AC7** Env forwarding through `CLAUDE_ENV`:\n85\t  - `grep -nE '^\\s+CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"$' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns exactly 1 line. This is anchored so a value that exists only in a YAML comment does not pass.\n86\t  - `grep -nE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns 1 line.\n87\t  - `grep -nE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns 1 line.\n88\t  - `grep -nE '^\\s+(GIT_REST_URL|PROMETHEUS_URL):' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns 0 lines (exit 1): the dead plain-env keys are gone.\n89\t\n90\t  Evidence: grep output and exit codes.\n91\t- [ ] **AC8** Allowlist, scripts and prose agree, checked by a test that parses `ALLOWED_TOOLS` from `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`:\n92\t  - Every `Bash(scripts/<name>:*)` entry names an executable file under `agent/scripts/`.\n93\t  - Every executable file under `agent/scripts/` has a `Bash(scripts/<name>:*)` entry.\n94\t  - Every `scripts/<name>.sh` mentioned in `pkg/prompts/*.md` or `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` has an entry.\n95\t  - Exact string: `grep -c 'ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:\\*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:\\*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:\\*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:\\*)\"' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` prints `1`.\n96\t  - Negative: `grep -ciE 'pod[- ]?logs' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md README.md pkg/prompts/*.md` prints `:0` for every file and exits 1.\n97\t\n98\t  Evidence: test assertions, grep output and exit code.\n99\t- [ ] **AC9** Read-only by construction (negative). Continuation lines are joined first, and only `curl` invocations are inspected:\n100\t\n101\t  ```\n102\t  sed -e ':a' -e '/\\\\$/N; s/\\\\\\n//; ta' agent/scripts/*.sh | grep -E '(^|[^A-Za-z_])curl ' | grep -cE -- '(-X|--request|--upload-file| -T |--data([^-]|$)|--data-(binary|raw|ascii)|--json| -d | -F |--form)'\n103\t  ```\n104\t\n105\t  This prints `0`. Separately, `grep -nE 'git (push|commit|remote)' agent/scripts/*.sh` returns 0 lines (exit 1). Evidence: output and exit codes.\n106\t- [ ] **AC10** No env knobs (negative):\n107\t  - `grep -nE 'REPO_CLONE_DIR|GIT_CLONE_DEPTH|GIT_CLONE_TOKEN|GATEWAY_SECRET' agent/scripts/*.sh` returns 0 lines.\n108\t  - `grep -nE '\\$\\{[A-Z_]+:-' agent/scripts/*.sh` returns 0 lines.\n109\t  - Both exit 1.\n110\t\n111\t  Evidence: empty output.\n112\t- [ ] **AC11** Image, hygiene and docs:\n113\t  - `grep -nE 'apk .*add.* git( |$)' Dockerfile` returns at least 1 line.\n114\t  - `grep -n '^/agent/repos/' .gitignore` returns 1 line.\n115\t  - `grep -c 'docs/observation-scripts.md' README.md` returns at least 1.\n116\t  - `grep -cE 'CLAUDE_ENV.*(GIT_REST_URL|PROMETHEUS_URL)' README.md` returns at least 1. The plain `CLAUDE_ENV` row already in the Env Vars table does not satisfy this.\n117\t  - `grep -c 'task files → Prometheus' README.md` returns 1, so the \"Observes\" line is rewritten, not deleted. This is a preservation guard and passes on today's README by design; the AC8 negative grep and the deferred-wording check force the actual rewrite.\n118\t  - `grep -c 'Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2'` returns at least 1 on each of `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` and `README.md`.\n119\t  - `grep -c 'ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env' README.md` returns 0 (today: 1, README.md:68). This removes the Go-threading advice however it is capitalised.\n120\t  - `sed -n '/^### Claude subprocess env allowlist/,/^## /p' README.md | grep -c 'CLAUDE_ENV'` returns at least 1, so the paragraph keeps its \"pod env is stripped\" warning and names the channel. Deleting the section fails this check. README's \"Claude subprocess env allowlist\" paragraph names `CLAUDE_ENV` as the channel for custom env, not a Go change.\n121\t  - `grep -n '(task files, Prometheus)' agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` returns 1 line.\n122\t  - `sed -n '/^## Unreleased/,/^## v/p' CHANGELOG.md | grep -ci 'observation scripts'` returns at least 1.\n123\t\n124\t  Evidence: grep output.\n125\t\n126\tOperator-executable:\n127\t\n128\t- [ ] **AC12** Env reaches the subprocess. Run from `cmd/run-task`, with the router token exported as `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`:\n129\t\n130\t  ```\n131\t  cp dummy-task.md /tmp/toolkit-ac12-task.md\n132\t  export CLAUDE_ENV=\"$(sed -nE 's/^[[:space:]]+CLAUDE_ENV: \"(.*)\"$/\\1/p' ../../k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\"\n133\t  go run . -task-file=/tmp/toolkit-ac12-task.md -branch=dev -agent-dir=\"$(cd ../.. && pwd)/agent\" \\\n134\t    -claude-config-dir=\"$HOME/.claude-agent\" -allowed-tools=Grep,Read \\\n135\t    -anthropic-base-url=http://127.0.0.1:8788 -anthropic-model=MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed \\\n136\t    -v=2 2> /tmp/toolkit-ac12.log\n137\t  grep 'cmd.Env =' /tmp/toolkit-ac12.log\n138\t  ```\n139\t\n140\t  The `cmd.Env =` line includes both `GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090` and `PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090`. That proves the **committed Config string** parses into both keys, through the same `env:\"CLAUDE_ENV\"` path the pod uses (not the `-claude-env` flag). The task file is a `/tmp` copy, because the file deliverer writes into it. No endpoint needs to be reachable. Evidence: log line.\n141\t\n142\t**Scenario coverage:** no new scenario. Every behavior here is reachable by script tests with a recording HTTP server and a stub `git`. The live journey is covered by scenario 001 and by the diagnosis spec's rung-1.\n143\t\n144\t## Verification\n145\t\n146\t### Container-executable (runs inside the YOLO container at prompt time)\n147\t\n148\t- `make precommit` (AC1)\n149\t- `make test`: script suites and the consistency test (AC2, AC3, AC5, AC6, AC8)\n150\t- The greps of AC4, AC7, AC8 (exact string + negative), AC9, AC10 and AC11, each with the stated count or exit code.\n151\t\n152\t### Operator-executable (host, after merge)\n153\t\n154\t- AC12 via `cmd/run-task` with `CLAUDE_ENV` exported from the Config value, then `grep 'cmd.Env ='` on stderr.\n155\t\n156\t**Doc edits that accompany this spec:** `docs/observation-scripts.md` (the authoritative script contract), `docs/verdict-gate.md` (used by the diagnosis spec) and `docs/dod.md`. The last is the `.dark-factory.yaml` `validationPrompt`, copied from `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer` with its dangling references removed. All three are committed together with the specs before approve.\n157\t\n158\t## Desired Behavior\n159\t\n160\t1. **HTTP read scripts.** `vault-read.sh`, `vault-list.sh` and `prometheus-query.sh` exist in `agent/scripts/`, are executable, and behave as `docs/observation-scripts.md` specifies:\n161\t   - GET only, with a 30 s timeout.\n162\t   - Stdout capped at 65536 bytes, with a `truncated` stderr marker and exit 0 when cut.\n163\t   - On an HTTP error, non-zero exit with the status on stderr.\n164\t   - Arguments validated before any request; a missing env var named on stderr.\n165\t\n166\t   That page is authoritative. The upstream scripts it names are informational only.\n167\t2. **Clone script.** `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>` behaves as `docs/observation-scripts.md` specifies:\n168\t   - `.` and `..` are rejected as owner or name.\n169\t   - As defense in depth, the resolved destination (symlinks followed) is asserted strictly inside `<agent dir>/repos/` before any `rm -rf` or `chmod`.\n170\t   - The clone root is the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/`.\n171\t   - Write permission is restored before an existing clone is replaced, and the tree is non-writable after cloning.\n172\t   - No submodules, no credentials, no `log` subcommand and no env knobs.\n173\t   - A failed `git clone` reports `git clone failed`.\n174\t3. **Env forwarding via `CLAUDE_ENV`.** The Config's `spec.env` gains `CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"` and loses the plain `GIT_REST_URL` / `PROMETHEUS_URL` keys, which nothing reads. Both entry points already parse `CLAUDE_ENV` / `-claude-env` into `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` (`main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go`, `ClaudeEnvRaw`), so no Go code changes. README documents `CLAUDE_ENV` as the path for script env.\n175\t4. **Config / image / prose consistency.**\n176\t   - The Config's `ALLOWED_TOOLS` becomes exactly `Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)`.\n177\t   - The Config's comments describe read path 3 as \"Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2\".\n178\t   - The Dockerfile's `apk add` line gains `git`, and `/agent/repos/` is gitignored.\n179\t   - `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` reads \"(task files, Prometheus)\".\n180\t   - README's \"Observes\" line becomes \"task files → Prometheus\", and path 3 is noted as deferred in the same wording as the Config.\n181\t   - README's \"Claude subprocess env allowlist\" paragraph is rewritten: custom env reaches the subprocess through `CLAUDE_ENV` (`KEY=VAL,…`), set on the Config, with no Go change.\n182\t   - README links `docs/observation-scripts.md`.\n183\t   - A test keeps allowlist, scripts and prose in agreement in all three directions.\n184\t\n185\t## Constraints\n186\t\n187\t- **Frozen tool names.** The four `Bash(scripts/…)` allowlist entries keep their exact names, resolved relative to the agent working directory. The Dockerfile's existing `COPY agent/ /agent/` ships them.\n188\t- **Script contracts** are frozen in `docs/observation-scripts.md`. A behavior change updates that page in the same change.\n189\t- **No Go change for env.** `CLAUDE_ENV` / `ClaudeEnvRaw` in both entry points stays exactly as it is.\n190\t- No change to the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module.\n191\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` keeps its \"NOT APPLIED\" header. Only `ALLOWED_TOOLS`, the env keys and the path-3 comments change.\n192\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` § Forbidden is unchanged. The scripts remain the sole exception to the internal-network rule.\n193\t- Existing tests keep passing, and the healthcheck / oauth-probe routing is untouched.\n194\t- **Assumptions:**\n195\t  - git-rest's glob listing (`GET /api/v1/files/?glob=`) is verified by the Sentry collector's live use.\n196\t  - git-rest's single-file GET (`GET /api/v1/files/<path>`) is documented in the git-rest README but not verified by live use.\n197\t  - Whether Prometheus `/api/v1/query` requires auth is unverified (contract page, 2026-09-27).\n198\t  - The YOLO container has `bash`, `curl` and a non-root user available for the script tests.\n199\t\n200\t## Failure Modes\n201\t\n202\t| Trigger | Expected behavior | Detection | Recovery |\n203\t|---|---|---|---|\n204\t| git-rest or Prometheus down / 5xx (external unavailability) | Script exits non-zero with the status on stderr | Model sees stderr; the diagnosis escalation names it | Operator restores the endpoint and re-assigns: `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent` |\n205\t| Prometheus requires auth (401/403) | Script exits non-zero with `401`/`403` on stderr | stderr | A follow-up spec adds auth forwarding |\n206\t| `CLAUDE_ENV` missing a key in the applied Config (drift) | Script exits with `<VAR> is required` | AC7 grep before merge; at runtime, the `cmd.Env =` log line at `-v=2` lacks the key | Fix the Config's `CLAUDE_ENV` value |\n207\t| Crafted repo reference or planted symlink (abuse) | Exit 2 before git runs or the filesystem changes | AC5; stderr `invalid repo reference` | None needed |\n208\t| Re-clone over a read-only tree as non-root | Write permission restored, then the old tree is replaced | AC6 second-clone case | None needed |\n209\t| Disk full / private repo during clone (resource exhaustion) | Non-zero exit, `git clone failed for <url>` | stderr | Diagnosis escalates. Private-repo auth is a Non-goal |\n210\t| Huge response (resource exhaustion) | Stdout cut at 65536 bytes, `truncated` on stderr, exit 0 | stderr | Model narrows the query |\n211\t| Endpoint hangs | curl aborts at 30 s with a non-zero exit | stderr timeout message | Re-assign the task |\n212\t| Rate limiting | Not applicable: git-rest and in-cluster Prometheus apply no rate limit to these reads | — | — |\n213\t| Clock skew | Not applicable: instant queries send no `time`, so Prometheus evaluates at its own now | — | — |\n214\t\n215\t## Security / Abuse Cases\n216\t\n217\t- **Attacker control:** script arguments come from the model, which reads untrusted task text and repo content. Every argument is treated as hostile.\n218\t- **SSRF / path abuse:**\n219\t  - `prometheus-query.sh` fixes the path to `/api/v1/query` and sends the argument only as an encoded query parameter.\n220\t  - `vault-read.sh` rejects absolute paths, `..` segments, `?`, `#` and `://`.\n221\t  - `repo-clone.sh` accepts only `github.com/<owner>/<name>` from a strict charset and rejects `.`/`..` segments. As defense in depth, it verifies that the symlink-resolved destination lies inside `repos/` before any destructive filesystem call. A reference cannot reach another host, `file://`, or a path outside the clone root.\n222\t- **Writes:** no `curl` invocation carries a write verb (AC9). The clone tree is non-writable and never pushed.\n223\t- **Trust boundary:** `CLAUDE_ENV` gains only `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL`, and neither is a secret. No token reaches the scripts.\n224\t- **Hang:** every HTTP call has a 30 s timeout. The clone is bounded by the Job's lifetime.\n225\t\n226\t## Suggested Decomposition\n227\t\n228\t| # | Prompt focus | Covers DBs | Covers ACs | Depends on |\n229\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n230\t| 1 | Three HTTP scripts + recording-server test suite | 1 | 2, 3, 4, 9 (curl part), 10 | — |\n231\t| 2 | `repo-clone.sh` with traversal + symlink guard + stub-git test suite | 2 | 5, 6, 9 (git part), 10 | — |\n232\t| 3 | Config `ALLOWED_TOOLS` + `CLAUDE_ENV` + comments, Dockerfile `git`, `.gitignore`, CLAUDE.md / README / CHANGELOG, three-way consistency test | 3, 4 | 7, 8, 11 | prompts 1, 2 |\n233\t| — | `make precommit` on every prompt; AC12 by the operator after merge | — | 1, 12 | all |\n234\t\n235\tRationale: the two script prompts are independent leaves. Prompt 3's consistency test needs every allowlisted script to exist and every script to be allowlisted, so it lands last.\n236\t\n237\t## Do-Nothing Option\n238\t\n239\tThe diagnoser has no working way to observe the running system, and its allowlist names tools that do not exist. Any diagnosis prompt would fail on its first read, or fall back to guessing from source, which the defect lane forbids. Spec `diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate` cannot ship without this one. Not acceptable.\n240\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9484eac8eb1e4e34","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"d19aba95-7979-49fb-bb33-a317a0584233","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:42:13.866Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bdd497d153ad23a9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Observation scripts — contracts\n2\t\n3\tThe diagnoser observes the running system only through these read-only scripts. **This page is the authoritative contract** for them; the upstream scripts they were ported from (named at the end) are informational only.\n4\t\n5\tThe Config's `ALLOWED_TOOLS` grants each script as `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)`, and Claude invokes them relative to its working directory (the agent dir, `/agent` in the image). They live in `agent/scripts/` and ship through the Dockerfile's `COPY agent/ /agent/`.\n6\t\n7\tContract source: [[Defect Lane Task Chain]] § Live observation — read path 1 (task files) and read path 2 (metrics). Read path 3 (Kubernetes API) waits on a platform change and has no script.\n8\t\n9\t## How the scripts get their env\n10\t\n11\tThe Claude runner passes only `HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,ZONEINFO,TMPDIR,LANG,LC_ALL` from the pod into the Claude subprocess. `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` reach the scripts through the existing `CLAUDE_ENV` channel (comma-separated `KEY=VALUE`, merged into `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` by both entry points):\n12\t\n13\t- in-cluster: Config `spec.env.CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n14\t- local CLI: `-claude-env='GIT_REST_URL=…,PROMETHEUS_URL=…'`\n15\t\n16\tAt `-v=2` the runner logs `cmd.Env = [...]`; both keys appear there when forwarding works.\n17\t\n18\t## Common rules (all three HTTP scripts)\n19\t\n20\t| Rule | Value |\n21\t|---|---|\n22\t| Method | `GET` only — no `-X`, `--request`, `-d`, `--data`, `--data-raw`, `--data-binary`, `--json`, `-F`, `--form`, `-T`, `--upload-file`; query parameters go through `-G --data-urlencode` |\n23\t| Timeout | `--max-time 30` |\n24\t| HTTP error | non-zero exit; stderr carries the HTTP status (e.g. `500`, `401`) — curl `-sS -f` or an explicit status check |\n25\t| Missing env var | non-zero exit; stderr names the variable (`<VAR> is required`) |\n26\t| Output cap | stdout capped at 65536 bytes; when cut, stderr contains `truncated` and the exit code is **0** (the cut must not surface as a pipefail / SIGPIPE failure) |\n27\t| Env | only the variable named below; no defaulted (`${VAR:-…}`) env knobs, no gateway secret, no tokens |\n28\t\n29\t## `vault-read.sh <path>`\n30\t\n31\t- One argument: a vault-relative file path.\n32\t- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: absolute path (leading `/`), any `..` segment (`../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..`), any `?`, `#` or `://`.\n33\t- Spaces are percent-encoded.\n34\t- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/<encoded path>`.\n35\t- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n36\t\n37\t## `vault-list.sh <glob>`\n38\t\n39\t- One argument: a git-rest glob (`filepath.Match` semantics; `*` does not cross `/`; `**` unsupported).\n40\t- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/` with query parameter `glob=<glob>` (URL-encoded).\n41\t- stdout: one path per line; empty when nothing matches.\n42\t- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n43\t\n44\t## `prometheus-query.sh <promql>`\n45\t\n46\t- Exactly one argument: a PromQL instant-query expression.\n47\t- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: an argument starting with `/` or containing `://`.\n48\t- Request: `GET ${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query` with query parameter `query=<promql>` (URL-encoded). The path is fixed; no other Prometheus path is reachable. No `time` parameter — Prometheus evaluates at its own now.\n49\t- Env: `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n50\t\n51\t## `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>`\n52\t\n53\t- The only subcommand is `clone`. Anything else (including `log`) → exit 2 with usage on stderr.\n54\t- `<repo>` accepts `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>[.git]`, `git@github.com:<owner>/<name>.git`, or `<owner>/<name>`. It is normalized to `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>`.\n55\t- Validation, before git runs or the filesystem is touched — exit 2 on failure:\n56\t  - `owner` and `name` each match `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` (so `bborbe/.github` is valid)\n57\t  - neither `owner` nor `name` is `.` or `..` (so `../x`, `x/..`, `x/.`, `./.`, `../..` are invalid)\n58\t  - **defense in depth:** the destination `<agent dir>/repos/<owner>/<name>`, resolved to an absolute path with symlinks followed, lies strictly inside `<agent dir>/repos/`. This is checked before any `rm -rf` or `chmod`, and catches a pre-existing symlink under `repos/` pointing outside it.\n59\t- Clone root is fixed: the `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` (`/agent/repos` in the image; `agent/repos/` in a local checkout, gitignored). No env override.\n60\t- Clone: full history, no `--recurse-submodules`, no credentials (public repos only in v1).\n61\t- Replacing an existing clone first restores owner write permission on the old tree, then removes it — so re-cloning over a read-only tree succeeds for a non-root user.\n62\t- After cloning, the whole tree including `.git` is made non-writable (`chmod -R a-w`).\n63\t- stdout (flat `key=value`): `clone_path=<absolute path>`, `head_sha=<sha>`, `default_branch=<branch>`.\n64\t- `git clone` failure (any non-zero exit, e.g. 128) → non-zero exit, stderr `git clone failed for <url>`.\n65\t\n66\tCleanup after a local run: `chmod -R u+w agent/repos && rm -rf agent/repos`.\n67\t\n68\t## Upstream (informational only)\n69\t\n70\tPorted from `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/vault-list.sh`, `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/repo-clone.sh` (whose `..` traversal hole this contract closes), and `trading/agent/trade-analysis/agent/scripts/vault-read.sh`. `prometheus-query.sh` is new. Where this page and an upstream script disagree, this page wins.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9484eac8eb1e4e34","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"05d6fc41-6c26-4542-bcb3-438df864cf0d","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:42:13.867Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-882bb2e0f42c4723","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-read-only-observation-toolkit\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t# Add the three read-only HTTP observation scripts\n8\t\n9\t<summary>\n10\t\n11\t- The agent image gains three read-only helper scripts the model can call to read task files and metrics.\n12\t- Reading one vault file and listing vault files both go through the vault's HTTP API with a GET only.\n13\t- Querying Prometheus sends exactly one instant query to the fixed query endpoint and nothing else.\n14\t- Each script refuses a malformed argument before it makes any network call.\n15\t- Each script names the missing endpoint setting on stderr instead of failing silently.\n16\t- An HTTP error surfaces its status code on stderr instead of looking like a successful empty read.\n17\t- A huge response is cut off at a fixed size, marked `truncated` on stderr, and still exits 0 so the cut never looks like a failure.\n18\t- Every HTTP call gives up after 30 seconds, so a hanging endpoint cannot stall a task.\n19\t- The behaviour is locked down by tests that drive the real scripts against a local recording HTTP server.\n20\t- Nothing outside the new scripts and their tests changes in this prompt.\n21\t\n22\t</summary>\n23\t\n24\t<objective>\n25\t\n26\tGive the defect diagnoser its first two \"eyes\" on the running system: three executable, read-only HTTP scripts in `agent/scripts/` — `vault-read.sh`, `vault-list.sh`, `prometheus-query.sh` — that behave exactly as `docs/observation-scripts.md` specifies, so that a later diagnosis prompt can read task files and Prometheus metrics without any tool that can write, delete, or reach an arbitrary host. The scripts are the security boundary: every argument is hostile input, and every failure must be visible rather than silent.\n27\t\n28\t</objective>\n29\t\n30\t<context>\n31\t\n32\tRead these before writing anything:\n33\t\n34\t- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — the **authoritative contract** for all three scripts. Read it in full. Where it and any other source disagree, it wins.\n35\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the guardrails prose that tells the model these scripts are its API.\n36\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` — the Config that will allowlist these scripts as `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)`. **Do not edit it in this prompt**; the allowlist change and the consistency test land in a later prompt.\n37\t- `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` and `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` — the repo's Ginkgo/Gomega test idiom (suite file, external `_test` package, counterfeiter not needed here).\n38\t- `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the container's execution rules.\n39\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega suite and spec conventions.\n40\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-precommit.md` — linter limits that apply to test files too (`funlen` 80 lines / 50 statements, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines max-len 100).\n41\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-security-linting.md` — gosec expectations (test files are excluded from gosec, so no `#nosec` comments are needed).\n42\t- `docs/dod.md` — the Definition of Done for this repo.\n43\t\n44\tTwo facts about the environment, both verified while writing this prompt:\n45\t\n46\t1. `pkg/scripts/` will contain **only** `_test.go` files in `package scripts_test`. That is a valid Go package: `go test ./...` compiles and runs it. Do **not** add a non-test `.go` file to \"complete\" the package.\n47\t2. The container sets `http_proxy` / `HTTPS_PROXY` in the ambient environment. `curl` honours them, so a loopback request to the test server would be sent to the proxy instead, the recording server would see zero requests, and every \"zero requests\" assertion would silently invert. The test harness must therefore construct the child environment explicitly (see requirement 9).\n48\t\n49\tCreate `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` with exactly this content. All three prompts in this spec share this one suite file — do not create a second one, and if it already exists with this content leave it untouched:\n50\t\n51\t```go\n52\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n53\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n54\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n55\t\n56\tpackage scripts_test\n57\t\n58\timport (\n59\t\t\"os\"\n60\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n61\t\t\"testing\"\n62\t\t\"time\"\n63\t\n64\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n65\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n66\t\t\"github.com/onsi/gomega/format\"\n67\t)\n68\t\n69\tfunc TestSuite(t *testing.T) {\n70\t\ttime.Local = time.UTC\n71\t\tformat.TruncatedDiff = false\n72\t\tRegisterFailHandler(Fail)\n73\t\tsuiteConfig, reporterConfig := GinkgoConfiguration()\n74\t\tsuiteConfig.Timeout = 60 * time.Second\n75\t\tRunSpecs(t, \"Scripts Suite\", suiteConfig, reporterConfig)\n76\t}\n77\t\n78\t// repoRoot walks up from the test's working directory until it finds go.mod.\n79\tfunc repoRoot() string {\n80\t\tdir, err := os.Getwd()\n81\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n82\t\tfor {\n83\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(dir, \"go.mod\")); err == nil {\n84\t\t\t\treturn dir\n85\t\t\t}\n86\t\t\tparent := filepath.Dir(dir)\n87\t\t\tif parent == dir {\n88\t\t\t\tFail(\"go.mod not found above \" + dir)\n89\t\t\t}\n90\t\t\tdir = parent\n91\t\t}\n92\t}\n93\t```\n94\t\n95\t</context>\n96\t\n97\t<requirements>\n98\t\n99\t1. Create `agent/scripts/vault-read.sh`, `agent/scripts/vault-list.sh` and `agent/scripts/prometheus-query.sh`.\n100\t\n101\t   - Each begins with `#!/usr/bin/env bash` and a one-line comment naming what it reads.\n102\t   - Each is marked executable (`chmod +x agent/scripts/*.sh`) — the allowlist entry `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)` resolves to a file the agent executes directly.\n103\t   - Do **not** use `set -e` or `set -u`. `set -u` would abort on an unset endpoint variable before the explicit check can print the variable name.\n104\t   - Do **not** write `${VAR:-…}` anywhere, and do not introduce any environment knob (no clone dir, depth, timeout, output cap, token or gateway secret). The spec forbids env knobs outright.\n105\t\n106\t2. Argument handling, in exactly this order and all of it **before any network call**:\n107\t\n108\t   a. `[ \"$#\" -ne 1 ]` → print the usage line to stderr, `exit 2`.\n109\t   b. Per-script argument validation (requirements 5, 6, 7) → print the rejection reason to stderr, `exit 2`.\n110\t   c. Endpoint presence: `[ -z \"${GIT_REST_URL}\" ]` (or `PROMETHEUS_URL`) → print `GIT_REST_URL is required` / `PROMETHEUS_URL is required` to stderr, `exit 1`.\n111\t\n112\t   Zero arguments and two-or-more arguments must both exit non-zero with zero requests reaching the server.\n113\t\n114\t3. Request shape. Send the response body to a temp file and keep the status in a variable — do **not** pipe `curl`'s body into `head`, because a pipe turns the cut into SIGPIPE and the truncation case would exit non-zero instead of 0. This is the shape, shown with the Prometheus URL and parameter; each script substitutes its own URL, its own parameter name and its own argument:\n115\t\n116\t   ```bash\n117\t   tmp=\"$(mktemp)\"\n118\t   trap 'rm -f \"$tmp\"' EXIT\n119\t   status=\"$(curl -sS --max-time 30 -o \"$tmp\" -w '%{http_code}' \\\n120\t     -G --data-urlencode \"query=${expr}\" \"${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query\")\" || {\n121\t     echo \"request failed\" >&2\n122\t     exit 1\n123\t   }\n124\t   ```\n125\t\n126\t   Rules that follow from it:\n127\t\n128\t   - `GET` only. Never pass `-X`, `--request`, `-d`, `--data`, `--data-raw`, `--data-binary`, `--data-ascii`, `--json`, `-F`, `--form`, `-T`, `--upload-file`. `-G --data-urlencode` is the **only** permitted way to send parameters — it is also the only way the read-only check (AC9) accepts.\n129\t   - `--max-time 30` on every `curl` invocation, spelled exactly `--max-time 30` (AC4 greps for that literal).\n130\t\n131\t4. Response handling, identical in all three scripts:\n132\t\n133\t   - Status other than `200` → write the status alone to stderr (so `500` and `401` each appear) and `exit 1`.\n134\t   - Non-zero `curl` exit (transport failure, timeout) → a message on stderr, `exit 1`.\n135\t   - Otherwise read the size as `size=\"$(wc -c < \"$tmp\")\"` and normalise it with `size=\"$((size))\"` (the arithmetic expansion strips the leading whitespace some `wc` builds emit).\n136\t   - `size` greater than `65536` → `head -c 65536 \"$tmp\"` to stdout, `echo truncated >&2`, `exit 0`. The cut must **not** be reported as an error.\n137\t   - `size` at or below `65536` → `cat \"$tmp\"` to stdout, `exit 0`.\n138\t\n139\t5. `vault-read.sh <path>` — read one vault file.\n140\t\n141\t   - Reject with exit 2 when the argument starts with `/`; when `\"/$path/\"` contains the full segment `\"/../\"` (this rejects `../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..` while still allowing a file legitimately named `a..b.md`); or when the argument contains `?`, `#` or `://`.\n142\t   - Percent-encode before building the URL: `%` → `%25` first, then space → `%20`. No other encoding is needed because validation has already excluded `?`, `#` and `://`.\n143\t   - Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/<encoded path>` with no query string.\n144\t   - Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n145\t\n146\t6. `vault-list.sh <glob>` — list vault files matching a glob.\n147\t\n148\t   - No argument-content validation: the glob travels as a query parameter, not as a path.\n149\t   - Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/` with the query parameter `glob=<glob>`, sent with `-G --data-urlencode`.\n150\t   - Env: `GIT_REST_URL`. The body is written to stdout unchanged (one path per line, empty when nothing matches).\n151\t\n152\t7. `prometheus-query.sh <promql>` — one instant PromQL query.\n153\t\n154\t   - Reject with exit 2 when the argument starts with `/` or contains `://`.\n155\t   - Request: `GET ${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query` with the query parameter `query=<promql>`, sent with `-G --data-urlencode`. The path is fixed — no other Prometheus path may be constructed, and no `time` parameter is sent.\n156\t   - Env: `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n157\t\n158\t8. Create `pkg/scripts/http_scripts_test.go` in `package scripts_test`, using the suite file from `<context>`. It must drive the **real** scripts through the **real** subprocess boundary. Do not re-implement any script logic in Go.\n159\t\n160\t9. Test harness contract:\n161\t\n162\t   - Run the script directly: `exec.CommandContext(ctx, scriptPath, args...)` — not via `bash <script>`. This is how the agent invokes it, and it exercises both the shebang and the executable bit. Use a `context.WithTimeout(ctx, 60*time.Second)`.\n163\t   - Build the child environment explicitly: `PATH` taken from the parent, `HOME` set to a temp directory (so a stray `~/.curlrc` cannot inject a proxy), plus **only** the endpoint variable under test. Never pass `os.Environ()` — the ambient proxy variables would route the loopback request to the proxy and make the recording server record nothing.\n164\t   - Recording server: `httptest.NewServer` whose handler records method, raw request path and raw query, and writes a configurable status and body. Guard the recorded slice with a mutex. Assert on the **raw/escaped** path (`r.URL.EscapedPath()`, or `r.RequestURI`): `r.URL.Path` is already percent-decoded and would hide an unencoded space.\n165\t   - Helpers: `newRecordingServer(t, status int, body string) (*httptest.Server, *recorder)` and `runScript(t, script, env map[string]string, args ...string) (stdout, stderr string, exitCode int)`. Resolve script paths from `repoRoot()`.\n166\t   - Keep every `It` body under ~60 lines by using these helpers; `funlen` (80 lines / 50 statements) and `gocognit` (20) apply to test files too.\n167\t\n168\t10. Test cases — all of them, mirroring the spec's AC2 and AC3:\n169\t\n170\t    **`prometheus-query.sh`**\n171\t\n172\t    - one argument → exactly one request, method `GET`, path `/api/v1/query`, `query` parameter equal to the argument; stdout equals the response body; exit 0.\n173\t    - argument starting with `/` → exit 2 and zero requests; argument containing `://` → exit 2 and zero requests.\n174\t    - zero arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests; two arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests.\n175\t    - `PROMETHEUS_URL` unset → non-zero exit and stderr contains `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n176\t    - `500` response → non-zero exit with `500` on stderr; `401` response → non-zero exit with `401` on stderr.\n177\t    - 100 KiB response body → stdout is exactly 65536 bytes, stderr contains `truncated`, exit 0.\n178\t\n179\t    **`vault-read.sh`**\n180\t\n181\t    - each of `/etc/passwd`, `../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..`, `a.md?x=1`, `a.md#x`, `http://evil/x` → exit 2 and zero requests.\n182\t    - `25 Tasks/x y.md` → the recorded raw request path is `/api/v1/files/25%20Tasks/x%20y.md`.\n183\t    - zero arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests; two arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests.\n184\t    - `GIT_REST_URL` unset → non-zero exit and stderr contains `GIT_REST_URL`.\n185\t    - `500` and `401` responses → non-zero exit with the status on stderr.\n186\t    - 100 KiB body → exactly 65536 bytes on stdout, `truncated` on stderr, exit 0.\n187\t\n188\t    **`vault-list.sh`**\n189\t\n190\t    - `* Tasks/*.md` → the recorded `glob` query parameter equals `* Tasks/*.md`, and the request path is `/api/v1/files/`.\n191\t    - zero arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests; two arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests.\n192\t    - `GIT_REST_URL` unset → non-zero exit and stderr contains `GIT_REST_URL`.\n193\t    - `500` and `401` responses → non-zero exit with the status on stderr.\n194\t    - 100 KiB body → exactly 65536 bytes on stdout, `truncated` on stderr, exit 0.\n195\t\n196\t    **All three**\n197\t\n198\t    - every recorded request is a `GET`, and every recorded path is under `/api/v1/files/` (vault scripts) or equals `/api/v1/query` (Prometheus script).\n199\t    - each script file contains the literal `--max-time 30` (AC4's grep, asserted from the test as well).\n200\t\n201\t11. Before finishing, re-run `<verification>` and confirm every line passes. Walk each test case in requirement 10 against the code and confirm it is actually asserted — a test that never asserts a status or a request count does not count as covering the case.\n202\t\n203\t</requirements>\n204\t\n205\t<constraints>\n206\t\n207\t- **Frozen tool names.** The four `Bash(scripts/…)` allowlist entries keep their exact names, resolved relative to the agent working directory. The Dockerfile's existing `COPY agent/ /agent/` ships them.\n208\t- **Script contracts are frozen in `docs/observation-scripts.md`.** A behaviour change updates that page in the same change. Do not change that page in this prompt.\n209\t- **No Go change for env.** `CLAUDE_ENV` / `ClaudeEnvRaw` in `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go` stays exactly as it is. No new flag, field or helper for the two URLs.\n210\t- Do NOT modify `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `.gitignore` or the `Dockerfile` in this prompt — the allowlist, the prose and the three-way consistency test land in a later prompt.\n211\t- Do NOT create `repo-clone.sh` in this prompt; it is a sibling prompt's deliverable.\n212\t- Do NOT add a `pod-logs.sh` or any pod-log/event read. That waits on the Config CRD gaining a service-account field and is an explicit non-goal.\n213\t- No env knobs of any kind in the scripts: no clone directory, clone depth, timeout, output cap, `GIT_CLONE_TOKEN` or `GATEWAY_SECRET`. These are invariants, not defaults.\n214\t- No private-repo clone auth, no git-rest gateway auth, no Prometheus path other than `/api/v1/query`, no Prometheus range query.\n215\t- Do NOT change the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module. No `go get`, no `go mod tidy` beyond what `make precommit` runs, never `-mod=vendor`.\n216\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n217\t- Existing tests must still pass, and the healthcheck / oauth-probe routing is untouched.\n218\t\n219\t</constraints>\n220\t\n221\t<verification>\n222\t\n223\tRun each command from the repo root. All must pass.\n224\t\n225\t```bash\n226\tmake test          # the new pkg/scripts suite runs here\n227\tmake precommit     # AC1 — must exit 0\n228\t\n229\t# AC4 — each of the three scripts sets a 30 s timeout (count of 1 or more per file)\n230\tgrep -c -- '--max-time 30' agent/scripts/vault-read.sh agent/scripts/vault-list.sh agent/scripts/prometheus-query.sh\n231\t\n232\t# AC9 (curl half) — no curl invocation carries a write verb. The pipeline must print 0.\n233\ttest \"$(sed -e ':a' -e '/\\\\$/N; s/\\\\\\n//; ta' agent/scripts/*.sh | grep -E '(^|[^A-Za-z_])curl ' | grep -cE -- '(-X|--request|--upload-file| -T |--data([^-]|$)|--data-(binary|raw|ascii)|--json| -d | -F |--form)')\" = \"0\"\n234\t\n235\t# AC10 — no env knobs, no defaulted env vars. Both must find nothing.\n236\t! grep -qE 'REPO_CLONE_DIR|GIT_CLONE_DEPTH|GIT_CLONE_TOKEN|GATEWAY_SECRET' agent/scripts/*.sh\n237\t! grep -qE '\\$\\{[A-Z_]+:-' agent/scripts/*.sh\n238\t\n239\t# the three scripts exist and are executable\n240\ttest -x agent/scripts/vault-read.sh && test -x agent/scripts/vault-list.sh && test -x agent/scripts/prometheus-query.sh\n241\t```\n242\t\n243\t</verification>\n244\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9484eac8eb1e4e34","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"5947d2c8-b430-452c-b765-731ce339cd4e","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:42:13.868Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
