{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad7edbe5bebe2f27","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-read-only-observation-toolkit\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t# Align the Config allowlist, image and prose, and enforce the agreement with a test\n8\t\n9\t<summary>\n10\t\n11\t- The Config's tool allowlist stops naming a script that cannot work and matches the four scripts that exist.\n12\t- The vault and Prometheus addresses now reach the model through the channel the runner actually forwards, instead of sitting in pod env where they were silently dropped.\n13\t- The dead plain-environment keys for those two addresses are gone.\n14\t- The Config's comments describe the deferred Kubernetes read path in the same words the README uses.\n15\t- The container image ships `git`, so the clone script can run at all.\n16\t- A local clone directory cannot be committed by accident.\n17\t- The guardrails and the README describe the two read paths that actually exist, and the README no longer advises a code change for something the Config already handles.\n18\t- A test fails the build if the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the prose ever disagree in any direction.\n19\t- The changelog records the change.\n20\t\n21\t</summary>\n22\t\n23\t<objective>\n24\t\n25\tClose the gap between what the Config claims and what the image actually contains. Today the Config allowlists five scripts, none of which exists, one of which (`pod-logs.sh`) cannot work on the current platform; it also sets the two endpoint URLs as plain pod env, which the Claude runner strips before spawning the model — so even a correct script would fail with \"variable is required\" while `kubectl describe pod` shows the variable set. After this change the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the prompt/guardrail prose agree in every direction, and a test enforces that agreement so the next drift fails `make test` instead of failing at runtime.\n26\t\n27\t</objective>\n28\t\n29\t<context>\n30\t\n31\tRead these before writing anything:\n32\t\n33\t- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — the **authoritative contract** for the scripts. Read the \"How the scripts get their env\" section in full; it names the exact Config value this prompt commits.\n34\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` — the Config being edited.\n35\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the guardrails prose being edited.\n36\t- `README.md` — the Env Vars table and the \"Claude subprocess env allowlist\" section.\n37\t- `CHANGELOG.md` — the file to append an `## Unreleased` section to.\n38\t- `Dockerfile` — the `apk --no-cache add` line that must gain `git`. Note the final stage is `FROM alpine`, which resolves to the earlier stage **named** `alpine`, so packages installed in that stage do ship in the image.\n39\t- `.gitignore` — the file to extend.\n40\t- `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go` — read them to confirm the claim that no Go change is needed: both already parse `CLAUDE_ENV` (`env:\"CLAUDE_ENV\"`, arg `-claude-env`) through `envparse.KeyValuePairs` into the runner's env map. **Do not edit either file.**\n41\t- `pkg/prompts/workflow.md`, `pkg/prompts/output-format.md` — the embedded prompts the consistency test scans for script mentions.\n42\t- `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` and `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` — the repo's Ginkgo/Gomega test idiom.\n43\t- `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the container's execution rules.\n44\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` — entry format and the required `feat:`/`fix:`/… prefix.\n45\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega conventions.\n46\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-precommit.md` — linter limits that apply to test files too (`funlen` 80 lines / 50 statements, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines max-len 100).\n47\t- `docs/dod.md` — the Definition of Done for this repo (it explicitly requires the CHANGELOG entry and the docs update).\n48\t\n49\t`pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` already exists from a sibling prompt in this spec and defines `repoRoot()`. **Leave it untouched**, do not create a second suite file (two `RunSpecs` calls in one package fail the build), and do not redefine `repoRoot()`.\n50\t\n51\t<!-- Two deliberate deviations from the spec's literal AC text, both preserving the AC's intent:\n52\t\n53\t     1. AC7/AC11 write the leading whitespace as `\\s`. `[[:space:]]` is used here instead:\n54\t        portable across grep builds and asserts the identical thing.\n55\t\n56\t     2. AC8's exact-string check is written in the spec as `grep -c '<allowlist>'`. Plain\n57\t        `grep` is BRE, where `*` is a quantifier — the pattern `Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*)`\n58\t        compiles to \"…vault-read.sh\" + zero-or-more `:` + \")\", which does NOT match the file\n59\t        and returns 0, so the AC's stated `1` is unreachable with that exact command.\n60\t        `grep -cF` (fixed string) returns the intended 1 and is verified to do so. -->\n61\t\n62\t</context>\n63\t\n64\t<requirements>\n65\t\n66\t1. **`k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`** — three edits, nothing else in the file changes. The `NOT APPLIED` header, the `metadata`/`spec` values, `taskTypes`, `resources`, `secretName` and the `ANTHROPIC_*` keys all stay as they are.\n67\t\n68\t   a. Replace the `ALLOWED_TOOLS` value. Old → new:\n69\t\n70\t   ```yaml\n71\t   # old\n72\t   ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/pod-logs.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"\n73\t   # new — the `pod-logs.sh` entry is dropped; the four surviving names are unchanged\n74\t   ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"\n75\t   ```\n76\t\n77\t   b. Delete the plain `GIT_REST_URL:` and `PROMETHEUS_URL:` keys from `spec.env` and add `CLAUDE_ENV` in their place. The `CLAUDE_ENV` line must be indented, end immediately after the closing quote (no trailing comment on that line), and hold exactly:\n78\t\n79\t   ```yaml\n80\t   CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"\n81\t   ```\n82\t\n83\t   Replace the surrounding comments so they explain the mechanism rather than the old state — the current comment still says the scripts are \"not yet written — domain work\", which is no longer true, and the current endpoint comments sit on the two keys being deleted. Say that the Claude runner strips pod env down to a fixed allowlist, so the endpoint URLs reach the scripts only through `CLAUDE_ENV`, a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list parsed by both entry points.\n84\t\n85\t   c. Rewrite the trailing comment block about read path 3. It must contain the exact phrase `Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2`, must keep the substance about the missing `serviceAccount` field and the gated RBAC, and must not contain the string `Pod logs` (the platform cannot read pod logs, which is why the script is being dropped). Keep `pods/log` out of the phrase \"Pod logs\" — describing the ServiceAccount's future permissions is fine.\n86\t\n87\t2. **`Dockerfile`** — add `git` to the existing `apk --no-cache add` line, keeping the rest of the package list and the trailing backslash intact. No other Dockerfile change.\n88\t\n89\t3. **`.gitignore`** — ensure it contains exactly one line `/agent/repos/` (leading slash, so it anchors to the repo root and does not shadow anything else). A sibling prompt may already have added it because its tests create the directory: if the line is present, leave it alone; if it is absent, add it; never duplicate it. Leave the other entries as they are.\n90\t\n91\t4. **`agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`** — one edit: the domain bullet that reads \"(task files, Prometheus, pod logs/events)\" becomes \"(task files, Prometheus)\". Nothing else in the file changes; the `## Forbidden` section stays exactly as it is, and the scripts remain the sole exception to the internal-network rule.\n92\t\n93\t5. **`README.md`** — three edits.\n94\t\n95\t   a. The \"Observes\" bullet (currently \"task files → Prometheus → pod logs/events via its own read-only service account\") becomes:\n96\t\n97\t   ```markdown\n98\t   - **Observes (read-only, in order):** task files → Prometheus (Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2)\n99\t   ```\n100\t\n101\t   The phrase `task files → Prometheus` must survive verbatim, and the deferred wording must be the same phrase used in the Config.\n102\t\n103\t   b. Rewrite the `### Claude subprocess env allowlist` section. Keep the heading verbatim. Keep the warning that the runner strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) so a variable visible in `kubectl describe pod` can still be absent from the subprocess. Replace the advice to thread variables through `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` in `main.go` — the string `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` must not appear anywhere in the file afterwards. Name `CLAUDE_ENV` as the channel: a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list set on the Config's `spec.env` (or `-claude-env` for a local run) and parsed by both entry points. Include one line that contains `CLAUDE_ENV` and both endpoints, for example:\n104\t\n105\t   ```markdown\n106\t   `CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n107\t   ```\n108\t\n109\t   c. Link `docs/observation-scripts.md` from the README — at minimum from the rewritten section, and add it to the `## Related` list.\n110\t\n111\t   Leave the generic `Tune ALLOWED_TOOLS per task shape` example table alone: it illustrates other agents' tool sets (`vault-write.sh`, `trading-api-read.sh`) and is not a claim about this agent.\n112\t\n113\t6. **`CHANGELOG.md`** — add an `## Unreleased` section above `## v0.0.0` with one bullet describing what was implemented. Follow `changelog-guide.md`: the entry needs a `feat:` prefix and must mention \"observation scripts\". Do not describe verification steps, and do not use the prompt filename.\n114\t\n115\t7. **`pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go`** (`package scripts_test`, using the existing suite file and `repoRoot()`) — the three-way agreement test. It must parse the Config rather than hard-coding a copy of the allowlist:\n116\t\n117\t   a. Read `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` and extract the `ALLOWED_TOOLS` value with a regex equivalent to `(?m)^\\s*ALLOWED_TOOLS:\\s*\"(.*)\"\\s*$`. Fail loudly if it does not match — a silently empty allowlist would make every check below vacuous.\n118\t\n119\t   b. Split the value on `,` and collect the entries matching `^Bash\\(scripts/(.+):\\*\\)$`, keeping the captured script name. Compare the captured names as plain strings — never by re-grepping the file, because a shell `grep` pattern containing `:*` is a BRE quantifier and would silently match nothing.\n120\t\n121\t   c. Assert that set equals exactly `{vault-read.sh, vault-list.sh, prometheus-query.sh, repo-clone.sh}`, so an emptied or renamed allowlist cannot pass vacuously.\n122\t\n123\t   d. For every allowlisted script name, assert `agent/scripts/<name>` exists and is executable.\n124\t\n125\t   e. Walk `agent/scripts/`; for every regular file with any executable bit set, assert an allowlist entry names it. This is the direction that catches a new script nobody allowlisted.\n126\t\n127\t   f. Read `pkg/prompts/*.md` and `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`; find every `scripts/<name>.sh` mention with a regex equivalent to `scripts/([A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\.sh)`; assert each mentioned name has an allowlist entry. This is the direction that catches prose pointing at a tool that does not exist.\n128\t\n129\t   g. Assert no case-insensitive match of `pod[- ]?logs` in any of: `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, and every `pkg/prompts/*.md`. This is the negative half of the agreement: the dropped tool must not linger in prose or comments.\n130\t\n131\t   h. Assert the Config's `CLAUDE_ENV` value — extracted with a regex equivalent to `(?m)^\\s*CLAUDE_ENV:\\s*\"(.*)\"\\s*$` — parses into both keys. Mirror the call in `main.go` (`claudeEnv := envparse.KeyValuePairs(a.ClaudeEnvRaw)`): read that line first to confirm the import path, the call form and the result type, then use the same call here and assert the map contains `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` with the values `http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090` and `http://prometheus.monitoring:9090`. This is the container-side guard for the seam that the operator-side acceptance check proves on the host: a Config value that greps correctly but parses into one key would otherwise ship.\n132\t\n133\t   Note that `README.md` is deliberately **not** part of check (f): its example allowlist table names scripts belonging to other agents.\n134\t\n135\t8. Keep every `It` body under ~60 lines; factor shared reading/parsing into helpers so `funlen` (80 lines / 50 statements) and `gocognit` (20) pass.\n136\t\n137\t9. Before finishing, re-run `<verification>` and confirm every line passes. Walk requirements 1–7 against the files you changed and confirm each exact string is present (or absent, where the requirement is a removal).\n138\t\n139\t</requirements>\n140\t\n141\t<constraints>\n142\t\n143\t- **Frozen tool names.** The four `Bash(scripts/…)` allowlist entries keep their exact names, resolved relative to the agent working directory. The Dockerfile's existing `COPY agent/ /agent/` ships them.\n144\t- **Script contracts are frozen in `docs/observation-scripts.md`.** A behaviour change updates that page in the same change. Do not change that page in this prompt.\n145\t- **No Go change for env.** `CLAUDE_ENV` / `ClaudeEnvRaw` in `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go` stays exactly as it is. No new flag, field or helper for the two URLs.\n146\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` keeps its `NOT APPLIED` header. Only `ALLOWED_TOOLS`, the env keys and the path-3 comments change.\n147\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` § Forbidden is unchanged. The scripts remain the sole exception to the internal-network rule.\n148\t- Do NOT add a `pod-logs.sh`, a pod-log/event read, or any replacement for it. It waits on the Config CRD gaining a service-account field and is an explicit non-goal.\n149\t- No `kubectl apply`, deploy, secret manifest or RBAC. The Config file stays NOT APPLIED.\n150\t- Do NOT change the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module. No `go get`, never `-mod=vendor`.\n151\t- Do NOT create or modify the scripts under `agent/scripts/` — they are sibling prompts' deliverables, and this prompt only reads them. Do not edit `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` or the sibling test files.\n152\t- AC12 (proving the env reaches the Claude subprocess) is operator-verified on the host after merge, against the router token and the committed Config value; it is not reproducible in this container. Do not attempt it and do not add it to `<verification>`.\n153\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n154\t- Existing tests must still pass, and the healthcheck / oauth-probe routing is untouched.\n155\t\n156\t</constraints>\n157\t\n158\t<verification>\n159\t\n160\tRun each command from the repo root. Every line must pass.\n161\t\n162\t```bash\n163\tmake test          # the consistency test runs here\n164\tmake precommit     # AC1 — must exit 0\n165\t```\n166\t\n167\t**AC7 — env forwarding (all four must pass):**\n168\t\n169\t```bash\n170\ttest \"$(grep -cE '^[[:space:]]+CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"$' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n171\ttest \"$(grep -cE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n172\ttest \"$(grep -cE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n173\t! grep -qE '^[[:space:]]+(GIT_REST_URL|PROMETHEUS_URL):' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml\n174\t```\n175\t\n176\t**AC8 — allowlist, scripts and prose agree:**\n177\t\n178\t```bash\n179\t# `-F` because the allowlist contains `(`, `)` and `*`, which plain grep reads as BRE metacharacters\n180\ttest \"$(grep -cF 'ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n181\t! grep -qiE 'pod[- ]?logs' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md README.md pkg/prompts/*.md\n182\t```\n183\t\n184\t**AC11 — image, hygiene and docs:**\n185\t\n186\t```bash\n187\tgrep -qE 'apk .*add.* git( |$)' Dockerfile\n188\ttest \"$(grep -c '^/agent/repos/' .gitignore)\" = \"1\"\n189\ttest \"$(grep -c 'docs/observation-scripts.md' README.md)\" -ge 1\n190\ttest \"$(grep -cE 'CLAUDE_ENV.*(GIT_REST_URL|PROMETHEUS_URL)' README.md)\" -ge 1\n191\ttest \"$(grep -c 'task files → Prometheus' README.md)\" = \"1\"\n192\ttest \"$(grep -c 'Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" -ge 1\n193\ttest \"$(grep -c 'Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2' README.md)\" -ge 1\n194\t! grep -q 'ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env' README.md\n195\ttest \"$(sed -n '/^### Claude subprocess env allowlist/,/^## /p' README.md | grep -c 'CLAUDE_ENV')\" -ge 1\n196\ttest \"$(grep -c '(task files, Prometheus)' agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md)\" = \"1\"\n197\ttest \"$(sed -n '/^## Unreleased/,/^## v/p' CHANGELOG.md | grep -ci 'observation scripts')\" -ge 1\n198\t```\n199\t\n200\t</verification>\n201\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85e728cba2d5235c","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933","uuid":"a5ef9522-da69