this prompt.\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [!] Inlined reusable pattern: the ~40-line Ginkgo suite bootstrap is inlined verbatim here **and** in `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md` (identical content). Recommendation 3 below.\n- [x] Existing project docs referenced in `<context>` (`docs/observation-scripts.md`, `docs/dod.md`)\n- [x] Existing coding-plugin docs referenced (`go-testing-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md`)\n- [x] Domain knowledge lives in `docs/observation-scripts.md` (authoritative contract), not inlined\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `docs/observation-scripts.md` § `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>` | Verified (exists; contract matches req 3/4/6/7/8/9) | Correct |\n| `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Verified (exists) | Correct |\n| `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` (allowlist already has `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)`) | Verified (exists, line 41) | Correct |\n| `.gitignore` (`/agent/repos/` absent today) | Verified (exists, 7 lines) | Correct |\n| `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go`, `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` | Verified (exist; inlined suite matches the `factory_suite_test.go` idiom exactly) | Correct |\n| `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Verified (exists) | Correct |\n| `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md` | Verified (both exist) | Correct |\n| `docs/dod.md` | Verified (exists) | Correct |\n| `Dockerfile` `COPY agent/ /agent/` | Verified (line 24) | Correct |\n| `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh` | To be created (dir does not exist yet) | Correct (creation step) |\n| `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` | To be created if absent; content byte-identical to prompt 1's | Correct |\n\n**Environment claims in `<context>` — all independently verified:**\n- \"`pkg/scripts/` with only `_test.go` in `package scripts_test` is a valid package\": TRUE — `go test`, `go build`, `go vet`, `go list`, `go generate`, `go test -cover`, and the repo's pinned `golangci-lint@v2.13.1` with `.golangci.yml` all exit 0.\n- \"the container sets `http_proxy`/`HTTPS_PROXY`\": TRUE — all four proxy vars are set to `http://127.0.0.1:8888`.\n- \"GNU find is available\" (req 13 `-printf`): TRUE — `/usr/bin/find` is GNU findutils 4.9.0; `-printf '%p %m\\n'` works.\n- Non-root assumption: TRUE — container uid is 1000 (`node`), so the permission-restoration path in the Second-clone case is genuinely exercised, not skipped.\n- `bash` + `curl` present: TRUE (`/usr/bin/bash`, `/usr/bin/curl`).\n- `git clone` creates leading parent dirs (so req 6's `mkdir -p` being confined to the replace branch does not break the fresh-clone path in production): TRUE — verified with git 2.39.5 cloning into a nonexistent nested path.\n\n**Verification pipelines exercised with GNU sed/grep:** the AC9 curl-half pipeline prints `0` on a curl-free script, and both AC10 greps find nothing on a compliant script — the `<verification>` block behaves as intended.\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| External test package + Ginkgo/Gomega suite idiom | `go-testing-guide.md` | Compliant (inlined suite is a byte-match of `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go`) |\n| Linter limits apply to test files (`funlen` 80/50, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines 100) | `go-precommit.md` | Compliant (req 17 mandates helper extraction and ~60-line `It` bodies) |\n| No test-only package-level mutable state (`var X` + `SetX()`) | `go-time-injection.md` | Compliant (none introduced) |\n| No HTTP handlers / factories / `fmt.Errorf` in the prompt's Go | `go-http-handler.md`, `go-factory-pattern.md`, `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | N/A (prompt's Go is test-only) |\n\n**Mechanical pattern-collision checks run:** `errors.Wrapf` in `pkg/` → 0 matches (no collision); repo already uses Ginkgo/Gomega in `pkg/factory`, `pkg/prompts` (prompt matches); no mocks inlined. No collision found.\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag that disables the shipped behavior (the script has no flags/subcommands beyond `clone`, per spec Non-goals)\n- [x] No config fields or tunable thresholds — the spec's Non-goals explicitly forbid a clone-dir/depth/timeout/output-cap knob, and req 1/5/constraints enforce \"no env override, no `${VAR:-…}`\"\n- [x] No \"future-proofing\" knobs. The only env vars introduced are test-harness inputs (`STUB_GIT_LOG`, `STUB_GIT_CLONE_EXIT`), which do not exist in the shipped script\n- No hits.\n\n## Critical Issues\nNone. The prompt is fully container-executable, its code references all resolve, the shared-file coordination with sibling prompts 1 and 3 is consistent, and the `hideGit: true` / operator-only checks do not fire.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n**1. Req 4 — the \"repos/ does not exist yet\" branch reads as if it drops the `repos` component** (line 126). Taken literally, the resolved parent becomes `<resolved agent dir>/<owner>` instead of `<resolved agent dir>/repos/<owner>`, which would make the success case fail the \"strictly inside resolved `<repos>/`\" test. The leading sentence (\"the destination `<agent dir>/repos/<owner>/<name>` … lies strictly inside the resolved `<agent dir>/repos/`\") pins the correct intent, and req 15's Success case would catch a literal misreading — hence Recommendation, not Critical.\n\nfind (line 126):\n```\n   - Resolve the parent: if `<repos>/<owner>` exists or is a symlink, resolve it with `cd \"<repos>/<owner>\" && pwd -P`; otherwise resolve `<repos>` physically (or the agent dir when `repos/` does not exist yet) and append the literal `<owner>`. Then append `/<name>` and require the result to sit under the resolved `<repos>/`.\n```\nreplace with:\n```\n   - Resolve the parent: if `<repos>/<owner>` exists or is a symlink, resolve it with `cd \"<repos>/<owner>\" && pwd -P`; otherwise resolve the existing ancestor — `<repos>` when it exists, else the agent dir — and append the literal `repos/<owner>` (so the result is `<resolved agent dir>/repos/<owner>` when `repos/` does not exist yet). Then append `/<name>` and require the result to sit strictly under the resolved `<repos>/`.\n```\n\n**2. Req 11 + req 15 Success — the `head_sha=` / `default_branch=` round-trip is never asserted with a value.** The stub exits 0 printing nothing for `rev-parse`, so both keys are always empty and the test only checks that the lines exist. A variable swap or a stray pipe in `head_sha=\"$(git -C \"$dest\" rev-parse HEAD …)\"` would pass. Have the stub emit canned values and assert them.\n\nfind (line 157):\n```\n    - for any other subcommand it exits 0 printing nothing.\n```\nreplace with:\n```\n    - for a `rev-parse HEAD` subcommand it prints `0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567` and exits 0; for a `rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` subcommand it prints `main` and exits 0; for any other subcommand it exits 0 printing nothing.\n```\n\nfind (line 173, within the Success case):\n```\nstdout carries an absolute `clone_path=` inside `<agent dir>/repos/`, plus `head_sha=` and `default_branch=` lines;\n```\nreplace with:\n```\nstdout carries an absolute `clone_path=` inside `<agent dir>/repos/`, plus `head_sha=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567` and `default_branch=main`;\n```\n\n**3. Suite-file duplication.** The same ~40-line suite bootstrap is inlined in both `prompts/1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md` and this file. Two verbatim copies drift independently, and any drift produces the \"two `RunSpecs` calls\" build failure the prompt warns about. Consider moving the bootstrap to a project doc (e.g. an appendix in `docs/observation-scripts.md`, or `docs/testing.md`) and referencing it from `<context>` in both prompts.\n\n**4. Req 16 — tolerate `chmod` failure when `agent/repos` is absent.** After a rejection case the directory may not exist.\n\nfind (line 183):\n```\n16. Cleanup: an `AfterEach` must restore write permission before removing the tree — `chmod -R u+w <agent dir>/repos`, then `os.RemoveAll`.\n```\nreplace with:\n```\n16. Cleanup: an `AfterEach` must restore write permission before removing the tree — `chmod -R u+w <agent dir>/repos` (tolerate failure: the directory is absent after a rejection case), then `os.RemoveAll`.\n```\n\n**5. AC9 git-half is a substring check, so it also fires on comments.** `! grep -nE 'git (push|commit|remote)'` (line 217) fails if the script carries an explanatory comment containing `git push`, `git commit`, or `git remote`. Worth a one-line caution so the executor does not self-trip the gate. Add after line 217:\n```\n# (the pattern is a plain substring check: keep comments free of the literal strings `git push`, `git commit`, `git remote`)\n```\n\n## Strengths\n- **Fully container-autonomous.** Every `<verification>` line runs inside the mounted repo with no cluster/PR/Docker capability, and I confirmed `make test` exits 0 under the repo's `hideGit: true` masking.\n- **Boundary-crossing contract test is the right shape.** The stub `git` is a real subprocess and the Success case asserts the exact argv (`clone https://github.com/bborbe/foo <expected dest>`) and the absence of `--recurse-submodules`, plus a filesystem-boundary assertion (`find <clone> -perm -u+w` prints nothing). This is level-2-style integration coverage of the `git` subprocess seam.\n- **The three \"verified while writing this prompt\" facts are all true** — I re-verified each (test-only package validity incl. golangci-lint v2, proxy env, GNU `find -printf`), which is rare and materially reduces execution risk.\n- **Anti-hallucination guard.** `<context>` explicitly states the upstream `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/repo-clone.sh` is unreachable and must not be guessed at — this removes the most likely failure mode (inventing upstream code).\n- **Failure-mode traceability is complete** for every clone-relevant row of the spec's table, and the security/abuse section's defenses (charset, `.`/`..` rejection, symlink-resolve guard before any destructive call, non-writable tree) all map to concrete requirements.\n- **Cross-prompt coordination is explicit and conflict-free.** The `.gitignore` line this prompt adds is also required by AC11 (assigned to prompt 3); prompt 3 handles it idempotently (\"if the line is present, leave it alone\"), so the two prompts cannot produce a duplicate line. The shared `scripts_suite_test.go` content is byte-identical across prompts 1 and 2, and both are idempotent, so either run order works.\n- **YAGNI-clean.** No opt-out flags, no tunable knobs — the spec's Non-goals (\"Do NOT add a clone-directory, clone-depth, timeout or output-cap env knob\") are enforced in req 1, req 5, and the constraints.\n\n## Summary\nThis is an exemplary prompt: all DoD sections are present and high quality, every code reference resolves, the environment claims are independently verifiable (and true), and the prompt is fully executable by the read-only container agent with no operator-only or git-masked verification lines. The only findings are wording and test-strength improvements — chiefly the req 4 parenthetical about a non-existent `repos/` directory and the unasserted `head_sha`/`default_branch` round-trip. Priority action: apply Recommendations 1 and 2 before approve.","usage":{"total_tokens":105362,"tool_uses":31,"duration_ms":657243},"uuid":"c25b70d6-3abf-4179-86b9-f34fe1564a98","session_id":"31f2fa85-d626-41fe-b66d-5257d5b0f933"}
