Prompts\n\n**Files created** (execution order `1` → `2` → `3`; prompts 1 and 2 are independent leaves, 3 depends on both):\n\n- `prompts/1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md`\n- `prompts/2-spec-001-repo-clone-script.md`\n- `prompts/3-spec-001-config-allowlist-and-consistency.md`\n\nAll three carry `spec: [\"001-read-only-observation-toolkit\"]` and only the `spec`/`status`/`created` frontmatter fields.\n\n**Decomposition.** The spec's own 3-prompt split was kept unchanged. Three deliberate deviations:\n\n1. **`.gitignore` moved from prompt 3 into prompt 2** (prompt 3 keeps an idempotent \"exactly one occurrence\" check). Prompt 2's tests create real clone trees under `<repo>/agent/repos/`; with the ignore line arriving only in prompt 3, a test run killed mid-spec would leave a nested clone for dark-factory to commit. AC11 still holds after all three prompts.\n2. **Test location decided**: a test-only package `pkg/scripts/` (`package scripts_test` only). Verified empirically that a directory with only external-test files compiles and runs under `go test ./...`.\n3. **Suite-file ownership**: prompt 1 creates `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` (with `repoRoot()`); prompt 2 embeds byte-identical content behind an \"if absent, create; if present, leave\" guard; prompt 3 references it. Two `RunSpecs` in one package fail the build, so this had to be pinned.\n\n**Two defects found in the spec's own acceptance commands** (creator's claims — see audit findings for adjudication):\n\n- **AC8's exact-string check** — creator claimed it cannot pass as written (BRE `*` quantifier) and substituted `grep -cF`. **Audit 3 found this reasoning is wrong**: the spec escapes the asterisks as `:\\*`, so the spec's command does return 1. The `-F` substitution works but its justification comment is untrue.\n- **AC7/AC11 spell leading whitespace `\\s`** (GNU extension). Prompt 3 uses `[[:space:]]`, same assertion, portable.\n\n**Empirical verification performed.** The creator built a recording HTTP server, a stub `git`, candidate scripts, and a scratch copy of the repo with the intended edits, then ran every `<verification>` command verbatim: AC4 → `1` per file; AC9 curl pipeline → `0`; AC10 → no matches; behaviour cases (500/401, 100 KiB → exactly 65536 bytes + `truncated` + exit 0, `25 Tasks/x y.md` → `25%20Tasks/x%20y.md`, all 11 AC5 rejections, symlink escape, second clone, exit 128); AC7/AC8/AC11 all pass against the scratch copy.\n\n**Open questions / residual risks surfaced:**\n\n- `envparse.KeyValuePairs` could not be grep-verified: `/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/` is empty in this container. Mitigated by pointing prompt 3 at the in-repo call sites (`main.go:141`, `cmd/run-task/main.go:85`) and requiring the executor to read that line first.\n- `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer` is not reachable from this container. Prompt 2 says so explicitly and forbids guessing or copying from it.\n- Prompt 3 requirement 7h adds an `envparse.KeyValuePairs` assertion beyond AC7's greps — flagged for the reviewer in case it should be dropped as scope.\n- AC12 is stated in prompt 3 as a negative constraint (operator-side, not reproducible here), not as an operator-procedure block.\n\n**No scenario prompt was emitted**: the spec says \"no new scenario\", and all four scenario-writing conditions fail.\n\n## Audit Findings\n\n### prompts/1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md\n\n# Prompt Audit Report: Add the three read-only HTTP observation scripts\n\n**File**: `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md`\n**Score**: 8/10\n**Status**: Good\n\n**Audit environment note:** `dark-factory config` is not installed in this audit container. Mount/workflow facts were derived from `/workspace/.dark-factory.yaml` (`workflow: direct`, no `hideGit` key) and `/workspace/.dark-factory.log`, which records the effective config: `hideGit=true hideGitSource=arg`, `validationCommand=\"make precommit\"`, `testCommand=\"make test\"`, `promptsInboxDir=prompts`. There are no extra mounts beyond the repo, so `/home/node/.claude/...` paths resolve inside the container image itself (verified present) rather than through a mount.\n\n## DoD Checklist\n- [x] `<summary>` present and plain-language (10 bullets, no paths/struct names/signatures)\n- [x] `<objective>` states end state\n- [x] `<context>` present\n- [x] `<requirements>` numbered and specific (11 numbered steps)\n- [x] `<constraints>` present\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable command\n- [x] All paths repo-relative or container-valid (no host-absolute, no `~/`, no `$HOME/`)\n- [x] No bare `git ` commands in `<verification>` (verified: prompt contains zero `git ` invocations; `hideGit=true` in `.dark-factory.log`)\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` (`make test`, `make precommit`, `grep`, `sed`, `test`, `!` only)\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox (not `prompts/in-progress/`)\n- [x] Filename not prefixed with a global `NNN-`; `1-` is the allowed multi-prompt ordering prefix\n- [x] Filename reflects the primary change (the three HTTP scripts)\n- [x] Status is `draft`\n- [x] Frontmatter is exactly `spec` / `status` / `created`; `spec: [\"001-read-only-observation-toolkit\"]` uses the canonical full-slug form\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n- [x] Spec failure modes addressed: 5xx → status on stderr (req 4 + tests); 401/403 → status on stderr (req 4 + 401 test); `CLAUDE_ENV` key drift → `<VAR> is required` (req 2c + tests); huge response → 65536-byte cut, `truncated`, exit 0 (req 4 + tests); hang → `--max-time 30` (req 3) plus a 60 s harness `context.WithTimeout` (req 9); clock skew → no `time` parameter (req 7). Rate-limiting rows are N/A. Clone-related rows belong to the sibling prompt.\n- [x] Security concerns addressed: SSRF (fixed Prometheus path, arg only as encoded query param), path abuse (req 5 rejection list), writes (req 3 GET-only list), hang (30 s), trust boundary (no tokens, no secrets).\n- [x] External calls specify timeout behaviour (`--max-time 30` on every `curl`; 60 s test context).\n- [x] Boundary-crossing contract tests: **exemplary.** The prompt mandates level-2 integration — `exec.CommandContext(ctx, scriptPath, args...)` (real shebang + exec bit) against a real `httptest` server, asserting the **escaped** path. Verified the assertions are achievable: `curl` preserves `%20` in the path and Go's `r.URL.EscapedPath()` returns `/api/v1/files/25%20Tasks/x%20y.md` while `r.URL.Path` decodes it (so the prompt's warning about `URL.Path` is correct and load-bearing).\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` in `<requirements>` or `<verification>`\n- [x] No cross-repo writes (no clone, no push, no `gh`)\n- [x] Container-autonomous: no `kubectl`/`docker`/`make buca`/PR/deploy steps, and no operator-vs-agent split. AC12 (the operator-only env check) is correctly excluded.\n- [x] Sibling entry points covered: the three scripts share the response-handling block, and the prompt says so explicitly (\"identical in all three scripts\") with a per-script test block for each.\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [x] No inlined reusable pattern that should live in a doc — with one judgement call: the ~40-line Ginkgo suite file is inlined in `<context>`. This is defensible and arguably correct, because it must be byte-identical across three sibling prompts that cannot commit; `<context>` also points at `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` as the idiom source. Verified the pinned content is a no-op for `gofmt`, `golines --max-len=100` and `goimports-reviser`, so it will not be rewritten by `make precommit`.\n- [x] Existing project docs referenced in `<context>`: `docs/observation-scripts.md` (authoritative), `docs/dod.md`\n- [x] Existing coding plugin docs referenced in `<context>`: `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md`, `go-security-linting.md`\n- [x] Domain knowledge that outlives the prompt lives in `docs/observation-scripts.md`, not inlined — the prompt explicitly defers to it and forbids editing it\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `docs/observation-scripts.md` (authoritative contract) | Verified | Correct — exists, contract matches every requirement (GET-only list, `--max-time 30`, 65536 cap, `<VAR> is required`, per-script rejection rules) |\n| `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Verified | Correct — exists; the \"(task files, Prometheus, pod logs/events)\" bullet it refers to is present |\n| `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` | Verified | Correct — exists; still carries the stale `pod-logs.sh` allowlist entry the prompt correctly refuses to touch |\n| `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` | Verified | Correct — the pinned suite file is a byte-for-byte structural match (std imports + dot-imports, `RunSpecs` call form) |\n| `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` | Verified | Correct — exists |\n| `docs/dod.md` | Verified | Correct — exists; is the repo's `validationPrompt` |\n| `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Verified | Correct — present in the container image (22 KB) |\n| `.../coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md`, `go-security-linting.md` | Verified | Correct — all three exist at `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/` |\n| `pkg/scripts/` (new, test-only) | Verified empirically | Correct — built a scratch module with only `_test.go` files in `package scripts_test`: `go list ./...` lists it, `go test -cover` reports `ok … coverage: [no statements]`, `go vet` clean. The prompt's environment fact 1 holds. |\n\n**Verification block validated end-to-end.** In a scratch copy of the repo the auditor implemented all three scripts exactly as the requirements describe and ran the whole `<verification>` block: `grep -c -- '--max-time 30'` returned 1 per file; the AC9 curl pipeline printed `0`; both AC10 greps found nothing; all three exec-bit checks passed. Then requirement 10's behavioural cases were run against those scripts through a real `httptest` server — every case passed (happy path, both `exit 2` rejections, zero/two args, unset env, 500, 401, 100 KiB → exactly 65536 bytes + `truncated` + exit 0, the 7 vault-read rejections, `25 Tasks/x y.md` → `/api/v1/files/25%20Tasks/x%20y.md`, the `a..b.md` non-match, and the vault-list glob). The requirements are implementable as written and the stated assertions are achievable.\n\n**Two prompt claims verified as TRUE rather than assumed:**\n1. *\"test files are excluded from gosec, so no `#nosec` comments are needed\"* — confirmed. gosec's `-tests` flag defaults to **false** (v2.22.2 source: `flag.Bool(\"tests\", false, …)`; v2.26.1 `-help` prints no `(default true)`), and a real `gosec@v2.26.1 -exclude=G104 ./pkg/scripts/...` run reported `Files: 1, Lines: 179` — it scanned `main.go` only, never the test package. This matters because `exec.CommandContext(ctx, scriptPath, …)` would otherwise trip G204.\n2. *\"The container sets `http_proxy` / `HTTPS_PROXY` … the loopback request would be sent to the proxy\"* — confirmed. `http_proxy`, `https_proxy`, `HTTP_PROXY`, `HTTPS_PROXY` are all set to `http://127.0.0.1:8888`, and a first curl probe returned `403 Filtered … Generated by tinyproxy version 1.11.1` instead of reaching the test server. Requirement 9's explicit child-env construction is not paranoia; it is required for the tests to work at all.\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| External `_test` package + Ginkgo/Gomega suite | `go-testing-guide.md` | Compliant — mirrors `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` exactly |\n| No `fmt.Errorf` / correct error wrapping | `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | Compliant — the prompt inlines no error wrapping at all (0 occurrences of `fmt.Errorf`; repo uses Ginkgo assertions) |\n| No test-only package-level mutable state (`var X` + `SetX()`) | `go-composition.md` | Compliant — none introduced; the recorder is an instance guarded by a mutex, passed by pointer |\n| gosec / `#nosec` discipline | `go-security-linting.md` | Compliant — verified above that no `#nosec` is needed |\n| Factory / HTTP handler / counterfeiter patterns | `go-factory-pattern.md`, `go-http-handler-refactoring-guide.md` | N/A — no production Go code, no interfaces, no handlers |\n| Pattern-collision checks | — | Clean: `errors.Wrapf` count in `pkg/` is 0, no `http.NewRequestWithContext` in `pkg/`, no `counterfeiter:generate` in `pkg/`, and the prompt uses Ginkgo (matching the 5 existing Ginkgo files) rather than `testing.T` table tests |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag for the behaviour the prompt ships\n- [x] No config field, threshold or branch beyond what the spec demands — every tunable is a frozen literal: `--max-time 30`, 65536, the fixed `/api/v1/query` path, the fixed `/api/v1/files/` prefix\n- [x] No \"future-proofing\" knobs — requirement 1 and the `<constraints>` actively forbid env knobs, and `<verification>` enforces it with two negative greps\n- [x] No invented test cases for non-existent flags\n\nThis is the cleanest YAGNI surface seen on a prompt of this size: the spec's Non-goals (\"Do NOT add a clone-directory, clone-depth, timeout or output-cap env knob … These are invariants\") are carried into the prompt verbatim and mechanically enforced.\n\n## Critical Issues\n\nNone. The prompt has no container-autonomy violation, no hideGit violation, no operator-only command in `<verification>`, no cross-repo write, no `go mod vendor`, and no stale code reference.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n**R1 — Helper `t` parameter type is unspecified, and both obvious choices fail to compile.**\nRequirement 9 gives helper signatures with a bare `t`, but in a Ginkgo `It` body the only handle available is `GinkgoT()`. Verified empirically that `GinkgoT()` implements **neither** `*testing.T` **nor** `testing.TB` (`ginkgo.FullGinkgoTInterface does not implement testing.TB (missing method private)`). An agent that guesses either will burn a compile-fix cycle in a prompt whose stated purpose is to remove guessing.\n\n- Old (requirement 9):\n  `- Helpers: \\`newRecordingServer(t, status int, body string) (*httptest.Server, *recorder)\\` and \\`runScript(t, script, env map[string]string, args ...string) (stdout, stderr string, exitCode int)\\`. Resolve script paths from \\`repoRoot()\\`.`\n- New:\n  `- Helpers: \\`newRecordingServer(t GinkgoTInterface, status int, body string) (*httptest.Server, *recorder)\\` and \\`runScript(t GinkgoTInterface, script string, env map[string]string, args ...string) (stdout, stderr string, exitCode int)\\`. Type \\`t\\` as \\`GinkgoTInterface\\` and pass \\`GinkgoT()\\` from the specs — \\`GinkgoT()\\` implements neither \\`*testing.T\\` nor \\`testing.TB\\`. Resolve script paths from \\`repoRoot()\\`.`\n\n**R2 — The prescribed child-env construction trips the `prealloc` linter, which `<context>` does not list.**\nRequirement 9 tells the agent to build the child env from a map; the natural `slice` + `append` form is flagged by `prealloc`, which the repo enables (`.golangci.yml`). Confirmed by running the repo's own `golangci-lint v2.13.1` config against a faithful implementation: `Consider preallocating childEnv with capacity 2 + len(env) (prealloc)`. `<context>` enumerates `funlen`, `gocognit`, `nestif` and golines but omits the one linter the prescribed shape actually trips.\n\n- Old (requirement 9):\n  `- Keep every \\`It\\` body under ~60 lines by using these helpers; \\`funlen\\` (80 lines / 50 statements) and \\`gocognit\\` (20) apply to test files too.`\n- New:\n  `- Keep every \\`It\\` body under ~60 lines by using these helpers; \\`funlen\\` (80 lines / 50 statements), \\`gocognit\\` (20) and \\`prealloc\\` apply to test files too. Build the child env as \\`childEnv := make([]string, 0, 2+len(env))\\` followed by \\`append\\` — a bare slice literal plus \\`append\\` in a loop fails \\`make precommit\\`.`\n- (Optionally also append `, \\`prealloc\\`` to the `go-precommit.md` bullet in `<context>`.)\n\n**R3 — The `vault-list.sh` glob assertion invites a raw-query comparison that cannot pass.**\n`curl -G --data-urlencode` emits lowercase percent-escapes and `+` for space. The auditor measured the actual raw query for `* Tasks/*.md`: `glob=%2a+Tasks%2f%2a.md`. Requirement 9 pushes the agent toward raw assertions (\"Assert on the **raw/escaped** path\"), and requirement 10 then says the recorded `glob` query parameter \"equals `* Tasks/*.md`\" — a literal reading against `r.URL.RawQuery` fails. The risk is that the agent \"fixes\" the script instead of the test, breaking requirement 3's `-G --data-urlencode`-only rule and AC9.\n\n- Old (requirement 10, vault-list block):\n  `    - \\`* Tasks/*.md\\` → the recorded \\`glob\\` query parameter equals \\`* Tasks/*.md\\`, and the request path is \\`/api/v1/files/\\`.`\n- New:\n  `    - \\`* Tasks/*.md\\` → \\`r.URL.Query().Get(\"glob\")\\` equals \\`* Tasks/*.md\\`, and the request path is \\`/api/v1/files/\\`. Assert the **decoded** parameter, not the raw query string: \\`curl -G --data-urlencode\\` emits \\`glob=%2a+Tasks%2f%2a.md\\`.`\n\n**R4 — The transport-failure branch is never exercised.**\nRequirement 4 specifies `Non-zero curl exit (transport failure, timeout) → a message on stderr, exit 1`, and requirement 3's snippet implements it as `|| { echo \"request failed\" >&2; exit 1; }` — but no case in requirement 10 reaches it. A connection-refused case is cheap (point at a closed port) and covers the branch without waiting 30 s.\n\n- Old (requirement 10, prometheus block):\n  `    - \\`500\\` response → non-zero exit with \\`500\\` on stderr; \\`401\\` response → non-zero exit with \\`401\\` on stderr.`\n- New: append a bullet — `    - unreachable endpoint (\\`http://127.0.0.1:1\\`) → non-zero exit with a message on stderr — this exercises the transport-failure branch, not the status branch.` Apply the same added bullet to the `vault-read.sh` and `vault-list.sh` blocks.\n\n**R5 — Cross-prompt helper-name collision risk in the shared `scripts_test` package.**\nRequirement 8 creates `pkg/scripts/http_scripts_test.go` and requirement 9 names three package-level symbols: `runScript`, `newRecordingServer`, `recorder`. The sibling prompt `prompts/2-spec-001-repo-clone-script.md` writes `repo_clone_test.go` and `stub_git_test.go` into the **same** `package scripts_test`, and its requirement 17 says it will use \"helpers for the snapshot, the stub setup **and the script invocation**\" — a near-certain `runScript`. The prompt set coordinates the shared suite file explicitly (\"do not create a second one\") and tells prompt 2 not to redefine `repoRoot()`, but nothing reserves `runScript`. A redeclaration is a hard `make test`/`make precommit` failure.\n\n- Old (requirement 8):\n  `8. Create \\`pkg/scripts/http_scripts_test.go\\` in \\`package scripts_test\\`, using the suite file from \\`<context>\\`. It must drive the **real** scripts through the **real** subprocess boundary. Do not re-implement any script logic in Go.`\n- New:\n  `8. Create \\`pkg/scripts/http_scripts_test.go\\` in \\`package scripts_test\\`, using the suite file from \\`<context>\\`. It must drive the **real** scripts through the **real** subprocess boundary. Do not re-implement any script logic in Go. Define the package-level helpers \\`runScript\\`, \\`newRecordingServer\\` and \\`recorder\\` here, exactly once: sibling prompts in this spec add files to the same \\`scripts_test\\` package and must reuse these rather than declaring their own.`\n- Note for the caller: the matching reservation should also be added to `prompts/2-spec-001-repo-clone-script.md`, which currently only reserves `repoRoot()`.\n\n**R6 — The pinned suite file must actually be *used*, or `unused` fails lint.**\nRunning `golangci-lint v2.13.1` against a package containing only the pinned `scripts_suite_test.go` yields `func repoRoot is unused (unused)`. Requirement 9 saves prompt 1 by mandating `repoRoot()` for script-path resolution, but the constraint is implicit and both sibling prompts depend on the same file.\n\n- Old (requirement 8, `<context>`):\n  `Create \\`pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go\\` with exactly this content.`\n- New:\n  `Create \\`pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go\\` with exactly this content. At least one spec in the package must call \\`repoRoot()\\` — the \\`unused\\` linter fails \\`make precommit\\` if the suite file is the package's only file.`\n\n**R7 (minor) — `docs/dod.md` in `<context>` advises `go mod vendor`, which contradicts `<constraints>`.**\nThe file the prompt tells the agent to read contains: *\"update the dependency (`go get <pkg>@<fixed-version> && go mod tidy && go mod vendor`)\"*, while the prompt's `<constraints>` say `never -mod=vendor` and `make precommit`'s `ensure` target runs `rm -rf vendor`. The prompt adds no Go dependency so the practical risk is near zero, but the two sections read as a contradiction.\n\n- Old:\n  `- \\`docs/dod.md\\` — the Definition of Done for this repo.`\n- New:\n  `- \\`docs/dod.md\\` — the Definition of Done for this repo. Ignore its \\`## Dependencies\\` mention of \\`go mod vendor\\`: \\`make precommit\\`'s \\`ensure\\` target runs \\`rm -rf vendor\\`, and this prompt adds no Go dependency.`\n\n## Strengths\n\n- **Traceability is exact.** Every sub-clause of AC2 and AC3 has a matching bullet in requirement 10, and each was verified assertable. AC4, the AC9 curl half and AC10 are each covered by a requirement *and* re-asserted from the test.\n- **The two hardest environment hazards were found and pre-empted.** The proxy-interception trap (verified real — tinyproxy returns `403 Filtered` for the loopback request) and the gosec/G204 trap (verified non-issue, but only because the prompt checked) are both called out with the mechanism, not just the rule.\n- **The verification block is genuinely container-executable.** Every line was run against a faithful implementation and all of it passes. No `git`, no `docker`, no `kubectl`, no `dark-factory`, no `scripts/*.sh` — exactly the shape that survives `hideGit=true` and the absence of cluster credentials.\n- **Boundary-crossing tests are at level 2, not level 1.** The prompt forbids re-implementing script logic in Go and requires driving the real scripts through the real subprocess boundary against a real HTTP server, asserting the escaped path.\n- **The authoritative contract is referenced, not paraphrased.** `docs/observation-scripts.md` is declared the tiebreaker and is explicitly excluded from the change set.\n- **YAGNI is enforced, not just respected.** Two negative greps in `<verification>` mechanically prevent env knobs from creeping back in.\n- **The `<context>` explains *why* for the non-obvious rules.** \"Do not use `set -u` — it would abort on an unset endpoint variable before the explicit check can print the variable name\" and \"do not pipe `curl`'s body into `head` — a pipe turns the cut into SIGPIPE\" are exactly the justifications that prevent an agent from \"improving\" the script into a failure.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is a strong, well-researched prompt: traceability is complete for the ACs it claims (2, 3, 4, 9-curl, 10), every code reference resolves, the verification block is container-safe and confirmed to pass against a spec-faithful implementation, and the boundary-crossing test design is exemplary. No Critical issues. The deductions come from six small specificity gaps that will cost the executing agent a cycle or two rather than ship broken code — the highest-value fixes are **R1** (type the helper `t` as `GinkgoTInterface`; neither `*testing.T` nor `testing.TB` compiles) and **R5** (reserve `runScript` in the shared `scripts_test` package, and mirror that reservation into prompt 2, or a redeclaration will fail `make test`).\n\n### prompts/2-spec-001-repo-clone-script.md\n\n# Prompt Audit Report: Add the read-only repo-clone script with a traversal and symlink guard\n\n**File**: `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-repo-clone-script.md`\n**Score**: 9/10\n**Status**: Excellent\n\n## DoD Checklist\n- [x] `<summary>` present and plain-language (10 bullets, no file paths / struct names)\n- [x] `<objective>` states end state + why (1 sentence, not step-level)\n- [x] `<context>` present (8 read-first entries + 3 verified environment facts + the inlined shared suite file)\n- [x] `<requirements>` numbered and specific (18 steps; exact paths, exit codes, stderr strings, code snippets)\n- [x] `<constraints>` present (copied from spec, incl. \"Do NOT commit\")\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable command (`make test`, `make precommit`, greps, `find`)\n- [x] All paths repo-relative or valid container paths (no host-absolute, no `~/`; `/home/node/.claude/...` is the mounted container config)\n- [x] No bare `git ` commands in `<verification>` — target repo has `hideGit: true` (confirmed: `.dark-factory.log` line 1 `hideGit=true hideGitSource=arg`; `/workspace/.git` is `/dev/null`). `grep -nE '^[[:space:]]*git[[:space:]]'` finds none. Additionally verified empirically that `make test` exits 0 in this masked-`.git` container (the Makefile's `$(shell git …)` failures for `VERSION`/`ROOTDIR` are non-fatal).\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` (no `docker`, `make build`/`buca`, `dark-factory`, `kubectl*`, `scripts/*.sh`, `gh`)\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox (not `prompts/in-progress/`)\n- [x] Filename not globally prefixed; `2-` is the documented multi-prompt ordering prefix (`^[1-9]-spec-\\d{3}-.*\\.md$` matches)\n- [x] Filename reflects primary change (`repo-clone-script` = the deliverable)\n- [x] Status is `draft`\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n- [x] Spec failure modes addressed (see mapping below)\n- [x] Security concerns from spec addressed (req 4 symlink-resolve guard + req 15 symlink-escape case; req 9 `chmod -R a-w`; AC9 git-half grep in `<verification>`)\n- [x] External calls: the script's `git clone` deliberately has no timeout — the spec's Failure Modes say \"The clone is bounded by the Job's lifetime\" and Non-goals forbid a timeout knob; the test harness has `context.WithTimeout(ctx, 60*time.Second)` (req 12). N/A, correctly handled.\n- [x] New string crossing a boundary has a contract test: the `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>` URL is asserted byte-exact in the stub `git`'s logged argv (req 11 + req 15 Success)\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` in `<requirements>`/`<verification>`\n- [x] No cross-repo writes (no `git clone <external>` + `git push`/`gh pr create`)\n- [x] Container-autonomous (no `kubectl`/deploy/PR/observability steps; no operator-vs-agent split)\n- [x] Sibling entry points: N/A — new script with a single `clone` subcommand; the one shared artifact (`pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go`) is explicitly addressed and its content is byte-identical to prompt 1's\n\n**Failure-mode → requirement mapping** (spec `Failure Modes` table, clone-relevant rows):\n| Spec trigger | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| Crafted repo reference or planted symlink (abuse) | req 4 (resolve-guard, no FS touch before it) + req 15 Rejections + Symlink escape |\n| Re-clone over a read-only tree as non-root | req 6 (`chmod -R u+w` before `rm -rf`) + req 15 Second clone (with uid-0 skip) |\n| Disk full / private repo during clone | req 8 + req 15 Clone failure (`STUB_GIT_CLONE_EXIT=128`) |\n\nThe other table rows (5xx/auth on git-rest/Prometheus, huge response, endpoint hang, `CLAUDE_ENV` drift, rate limiting, clock skew) belong to prompts 1/3 or are \"Not applicable\" — none are silently dropped by this prompt.\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [!] Inlined reusable pattern: the ~40-line Ginkgo suite bootstrap is inlined verbatim here **and** in `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md` (identical content). Recommendation 3 below.\n- [x] Existing project docs referenced in `<context>` (`docs/observation-scripts.md`, `docs/dod.md`)\n- [x] Existing coding-plugin docs referenced (`go-testing-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md`)\n- [x] Domain knowledge lives in `docs/observation-scripts.md` (authoritative contract), not inlined\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| `docs/observation-scripts.md` § `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>` | Verified (exists; contract matches req 3/4/6/7/8/9) | Correct |\n| `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Verified (exists) | Correct |\n| `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` (allowlist already has `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)`) | Verified (exists, line 41) | Correct |\n| `.gitignore` (`/agent/repos/` absent today) | Verified (exists, 7 lines) | Correct |\n| `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go`, `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` | Verified (exist; inlined suite matches the `factory_suite_test.go` idiom exactly) | Correct |\n| `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | Verified (exists) | Correct |\n| `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md` | Verified (both exist) | Correct |\n| `docs/dod.md` | Verified (exists) | Correct |\n| `Dockerfile` `COPY agent/ /agent/` | Verified (line 24) | Correct |\n| `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh` | To be created (dir does not exist yet) | Correct (creation step) |\n| `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` | To be created if absent; content byte-identical to prompt 1's | Correct |\n\n**Environment claims in `<context>` — all independently verified:**\n- \"`pkg/scripts/` with only `_test.go` in `package scripts_test` is a valid package\": TRUE — `go test`, `go build`, `go vet`, `go list`, `go generate`, `go test -cover`, and the repo's pinned `golangci-lint@v2.13.1` with `.golangci.yml` all exit 0.\n- \"the container sets `http_proxy`/`HTTPS_PROXY`\": TRUE — all four proxy vars are set to `http://127.0.0.1:8888`.\n- \"GNU find is available\" (req 13 `-printf`): TRUE — `/usr/bin/find` is GNU findutils 4.9.0; `-printf '%p %m\\n'` works.\n- Non-root assumption: TRUE — container uid is 1000 (`node`), so the permission-restoration path in the Second-clone case is genuinely exercised, not skipped.\n- `bash` + `curl` present