.\n\n## Critical Issues\nNone. The prompt is fully container-executable, its code references all resolve, the shared-file coordination with sibling prompts 1 and 3 is consistent, and the `hideGit: true` / operator-only checks do not fire.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n**1. Req 4 — the \"repos/ does not exist yet\" branch reads as if it drops the `repos` component** (line 126). Taken literally, the resolved parent becomes `<resolved agent dir>/<owner>` instead of `<resolved agent dir>/repos/<owner>`, which would make the success case fail the \"strictly inside resolved `<repos>/`\" test. The leading sentence (\"the destination `<agent dir>/repos/<owner>/<name>` … lies strictly inside the resolved `<agent dir>/repos/`\") pins the correct intent, and req 15's Success case would catch a literal misreading — hence Recommendation, not Critical.\n\nfind (line 126):\n```\n   - Resolve the parent: if `<repos>/<owner>` exists or is a symlink, resolve it with `cd \"<repos>/<owner>\" && pwd -P`; otherwise resolve `<repos>` physically (or the agent dir when `repos/` does not exist yet) and append the literal `<owner>`. Then append `/<name>` and require the result to sit under the resolved `<repos>/`.\n```\nreplace with:\n```\n   - Resolve the parent: if `<repos>/<owner>` exists or is a symlink, resolve it with `cd \"<repos>/<owner>\" && pwd -P`; otherwise resolve the existing ancestor — `<repos>` when it exists, else the agent dir — and append the literal `repos/<owner>` (so the result is `<resolved agent dir>/repos/<owner>` when `repos/` does not exist yet). Then append `/<name>` and require the result to sit strictly under the resolved `<repos>/`.\n```\n\n**2. Req 11 + req 15 Success — the `head_sha=` / `default_branch=` round-trip is never asserted with a value.** The stub exits 0 printing nothing for `rev-parse`, so both keys are always empty and the test only checks that the lines exist. A variable swap or a stray pipe in `head_sha=\"$(git -C \"$dest\" rev-parse HEAD …)\"` would